'','A',0.5,'',0),(26,'&lt;p&gt;The boy ate his food hungrily. The underlined word is an adverb of _______&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nmanner&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;degree&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;frequency&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;time&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(27,'&lt;p&gt;Which of the following is an example of a literary genre?&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Grammar&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;. Prose&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Sentence structure&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Punctuation&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(28,'&lt;p&gt;Choose the correctly spelt word.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Embarras&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Embarass&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Embarrass&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nEmbaras&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(29,'&lt;p&gt;Which of the following features is essential in a formal letter?&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Slangs&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Two&lt;br /&gt;\naddresses&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;casual language. The use of emojis&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;casual language&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(30,'&lt;p&gt;&amp;lsquo;Mr Frama bought five fried fish from the fish seller&amp;rsquo; is an example of___&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Simile&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Metaphor&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Rhyme&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Alliteration&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(31,'&lt;p&gt;Which of the options is common to both formal and informal letters?&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A. Two&lt;br /&gt;\naddresses&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Conclusion&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Address of the receiver&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Signature after the subscript&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(37,'&lt;p&gt;A figure of speech that expresses an unpleasant thing in a pleasant way is&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\neuphemism&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;hyperbole&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;. irony&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;. metaphor&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(38,'&lt;p&gt;What literary device is often used to create a rhythmic pattern in poetry?&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Simile&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Metaphor&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Rhyme&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Alliteration&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(39,'&lt;p&gt;Choose the appropriate sentence from the following options.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;David&amp;rsquo;s shirt is white&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;. David shirt is white&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;David shirt is white&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Davids&amp;rsquo; shirt is white.&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(40,'&lt;p&gt;.The rain will prevent me from attending the party. The underlined word FROM is an example&lt;br /&gt;\nof ________&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;pronoun&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;verb&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;noun&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;preposition&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(41,'&lt;p&gt;When someone is accused of breaking the ___ (36)_, they must appear in a ___&lt;br /&gt;\n(37)___ to explain what happened. The __ (38)_ is in charge of making sure everything&lt;br /&gt;\nis fair and legal during the trial. Every person has the right to a fair hearing, which is&lt;br /&gt;\nknown as due process.&lt;br /&gt;\nThe court must have the right to hear a case. After listening to the evidence, the judge&lt;br /&gt;\nor jury gives a final decision, known as the __ (39)_. If someone is not happy with this&lt;br /&gt;\ndecision, they can ask for an appeal at a higher court.&lt;br /&gt;\nEach person can get help from a lawyer, who is trained to speak and defend them in&lt;br /&gt;\ncourt. No matter who you are, the law says everyone must be treated fairly. This is&lt;br /&gt;\ncalled _40_&lt;br /&gt;\n36&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;rule&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;law&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;order&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;warning&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(42,'&lt;p&gt;When someone is accused of breaking the ___ (36)_, they must appear in a ___&lt;br /&gt;\n(37)___ to explain what happened. The __ (38)_ is in charge of making sure everything&lt;br /&gt;\nis fair and legal during the trial. Every person has the right to a fair hearing, which is&lt;br /&gt;\nknown as due process.&lt;br /&gt;\nThe court must have the right to hear a case. After listening to the evidence, the judge&lt;br /&gt;\nor jury gives a final decision, known as the __ (39)_. If someone is not happy with this&lt;br /&gt;\ndecision, they can ask for an appeal at a higher court.&lt;br /&gt;\nEach person can get help from a lawyer, who is trained to speak and defend them in&lt;br /&gt;\ncourt. No matter who you are, the law says everyone must be treated fairly. This is&lt;br /&gt;\ncalled __ (40)_&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n37&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;library&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;church&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;court&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;school&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(43,'&lt;p&gt;When someone is accused of breaking the ___ (36)_, they must appear in a ___&lt;br /&gt;\n(37)___ to explain what happened. The __ (38)_ is in charge of making sure everything&lt;br /&gt;\nis fair and legal during the trial. Every person has the right to a fair hearing, which is&lt;br /&gt;\nknown as due process.&lt;br /&gt;\nThe court must have the right to hear a case. After listening to the evidence, the judge&lt;br /&gt;\nor jury gives a final decision, known as the __ (39)_. If someone is not happy with this&lt;br /&gt;\ndecision, they can ask for an appeal at a higher court.&lt;br /&gt;\nEach person can get help from a lawyer, who is trained to speak and defend them in&lt;br /&gt;\ncourt. No matter who you are, the law says everyone must be treated fairly. This is&lt;br /&gt;\ncalled __ (40)_&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n38&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;lawyer&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;police&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;teacher&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;judge&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(44,'&lt;p&gt;When someone is accused of breaking the ___ (36)_, they must appear in a ___&lt;br /&gt;\n(37)___ to explain what happened. The __ (38)_ is in charge of making sure everything&lt;br /&gt;\nis fair and legal during the trial. Every person has the right to a fair hearing, which is&lt;br /&gt;\nknown as due process.&lt;br /&gt;\nThe court must have the right to hear a case. After listening to the evidence, the judge&lt;br /&gt;\nor jury gives a final decision, known as the __ (39)_. If someone is not happy with this&lt;br /&gt;\ndecision, they can ask for an appeal at a higher court.&lt;br /&gt;\nEach person can get help from a lawyer, who is trained to speak and defend them in&lt;br /&gt;\ncourt. No matter who you are, the law says everyone must be treated fairly. This is&lt;br /&gt;\ncalled __ (40)_&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n39&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;result&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;plan&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;verdict&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;penalty&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(46,'&lt;p&gt;When someone is accused of breaking the ___ (36)_, they must appear in a ___&lt;br /&gt;\n(37)___ to explain what happened. The __ (38)_ is in charge of making sure everything&lt;br /&gt;\nis fair and legal during the trial. Every person has the right to a fair hearing, which is&lt;br /&gt;\nknown as due process.&lt;br /&gt;\nThe court must have the right to hear a case. After listening to the evidence, the judge&lt;br /&gt;\nor jury gives a final decision, known as the __ (39)_. If someone is not happy with this&lt;br /&gt;\ndecision, they can ask for an appeal at a higher court.&lt;br /&gt;\nEach person can get help from a lawyer, who is trained to speak and defend them in&lt;br /&gt;\ncourt. No matter who you are, the law says everyone must be treated fairly. This is&lt;br /&gt;\ncalled __ (40)_&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n40&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;justice&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Mercy&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;kindness&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;fairness&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(47,'&lt;p&gt;We requested for the menu at the _______.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;airport&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;castle&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;museum&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nrestaurant&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(48,'&lt;p&gt;The cook ___ the butter before frying the fish.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;crumbled&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;dissolved&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\ngrilled&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;melted&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(49,'&lt;p&gt;Choose the correctly spelt word:&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Definitely&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Definately&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Definitley&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nDefanitely&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(50,'&lt;p&gt;The doctor kept the sick boy under ______.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;inspection&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;monitoring&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nobservation&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;restriction&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(51,'&lt;p&gt;The part of the computer that is responsible for display is known as the________ ?&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;monitor&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;LED&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Core Processing Unit&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Central Power Unit&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(52,'&lt;p&gt;The poet of the poem, &amp;lsquo;Wind&amp;rsquo; is ____&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Rahila Diji&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Okesiji David&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Chinua&lt;br /&gt;\nAchebe&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Nicole Daniel&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(53,'&lt;p&gt;How many lines does a sonnet have?&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;16&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;20&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;15&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;14&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(54,'&lt;p&gt;According to the poet in &amp;lsquo;Diversity&amp;rsquo;, our diversity is_____ by God.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;organised&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;chosen&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;arranged&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;planned&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(55,'&lt;p&gt;Why can&amp;#39;t we plainly see? The figure of speech used in this sentence is ____&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nSimile&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Personification&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Rhetorical question&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;Contrast&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(56,'&lt;p&gt;According to the poem, the only thing that can make the world joyous is_______.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\nacceptance of our diversity&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;going our different ways&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;division&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;sharing the&lt;br /&gt;\nresource equally.&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(57,'&lt;p&gt;/ʊə/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;dear&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;foil&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;pear&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;pure&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(58,'&lt;p&gt;/aʊ/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;black&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;bound&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;bowl&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;laundry&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(59,'&lt;p&gt;/f/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;happy&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;have&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;page&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;photo&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(61,'&lt;p&gt;/e/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;bread&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;dew&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;people&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;real&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(62,'&lt;p&gt;/k/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;ache&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;branch&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;knee&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;knit&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(63,'&lt;p&gt;/u:/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;book&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;deep&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;good&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;cool&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(64,'&lt;p&gt;/ↄi/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;air&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;coin&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;court&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;rod&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(65,'&lt;p&gt;/ə/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;fame&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;doctor&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;hour&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;zip&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(66,'&lt;p&gt;/h/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;harmony&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;hour&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;heir&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;question&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(67,'&lt;p&gt;/ŋ/&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;may&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;nose&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;sing&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;laugh&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0);
