INSERT INTO `3rdtmb7agricexamsquest857` VALUES (1,'1.????? Agriculture is derived from two Latin words, ?ager? and ?cultura? mean A. land and cultivation. B. soil and land C. cultural and heaps D. ridges and land','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',1),(2,'1.????? The stone age is divided into  A. 2 periods B. 3 periods C. 4 periods D. 5 periods  ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',2),(3,'1.????? Nomadic herdsmen move their animals in search of A. cassava B. forage C. oil D. yam','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',3),(4,'1.????? An example of agro-allied industries is A. cement industry B. mining industry C. refinery D. textile industry ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',4),(5,'1.????? One of the following is used for medicinal purpose and also as stimulant A. cocoa B. tobacco C. pear D. melon ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',5),(6,'1.????? The following are characteristics of mammals except a. they do breast feed their young ones b. their body is covered with feathers c. they give birth to their young one alive d. they get pregnant ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',6),(7,'1.????? The farming of both plants and animals is called A. mono-cropping B. mixed farming C. mixed cropping D. pastoral farming ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',7),(8,'1.????? A crop which stores food in its leaf is A. onions B. cassava C. maize D. sugarcane','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',8),(9,'1.????? Biennial crops complete their lifecycle in A. two years  B.above two years C. less than years D. None of the above','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',9),(10,'1.????? The early men engaged in the following agricultural system except A. commercial farming B. fruit gathering C. hunting of games D. nomadic  herding','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',10),(11,'1.????? The science of growing  vegetables such as leafy vegetables is known as A. apiculture B forestry C. horticulture D. olericulture','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',11),(12,'1.????? Agriculture provides employment for the following individuals except A. research officers B. extension agents C farm workers D gold digger','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',12),(13,'1.????? Which of the following crops has leaves with net venation? A. barley B. cowpea C. millet D. sorghum ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',13),(14,'1.????? Crops can be classified according to the following except A. sources of essential food needs B. colour of seed C. uses D. lifespan','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',14),(15,'1.????? Dairy cattle are reared for A.beef B. manure C. Milk production D. transportation.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',15),(16,'1.????? Which of these animals are often kept with cattle by Fulanis in Nigeria. A. cats B. pig C. sheep. D. rabbits','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',16),(17,'1.?????  Which of these animals can be used in pulling a plough A. cattle. B. goats. C. rabbits. D. swine. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',17),(18,'1.?????  Which of these is not classified as poultry A. Duck. B. Eagle. C. goose. D. turkey.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',18),(19,'1.?????  Animals kept for companionship are called A. dairy animals. B. fattening animals. C. guard animals. D pets.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',19),(20,'1.????? Guard animals should posses all the following except A. beautiful coat colour. B. brave and fearless. C. curious. D. intelligent.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',20),(21,'1.????? Work animals are used for the following except  A. carrying load. B. harrowing. C. planting crops. D ploughing.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',21),(22,'1.????? Farm animals provide the following to man except(a)furniture (b) transportation (c) security (d) sport','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',22),(23,'1.????? The major reason why livestock rearing is high in northern Nigeria is because (a)consumers of meat are more in the north (b) grass pasture is abundant in the north (c)livestock survive more under high temperature (d) Northern government policy favours animal rearing','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',23),(24,'1.?????  Animals that live in water are (a) pets (b) aquatic animals (c) work animals (d) show animals.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',24),(25,'1.?????  Which of these is not a form of farm animals(a) Pet (b) Horse (c) Guard animals (d) Poultry.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',25),(26,'1.????? Animals that are reared for different purpose on the farm are known as (A) Wild animal (b) Domestic animal (c) Farm animal (d) Pet animals.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',26),(27,'1.????? Which of the following is a non-mammal a. cow b. duck c. goat d. pig','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',27),(28,'1.????? Which of the following is a mono-gastric animal a. cowb. rabbit c. goat d. camel','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',28),(29,'1.????? The largest stomach compartment of a ruminant is the?.. a. rumen b. reticulum c. omasum d. abomasum','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',29),(30,'1.????? The habit of bringing back already swallowed food into the mouth for proper chewing is termed a. vomiting b. rumination c. synthesize d. digestion','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',30),(31,'1.????? A bullock is a (a) castrated bull (b) castrated chicken (c) female dog (d) layer','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',31),(32,'1.????? The botanical name of carpet grass is ___________ (a) Cynodondactylon (b) Axonopuscompressus (c) Boerhivadiffusa (d) Chromolaena odorata','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',32),(33,'1.????? Which of the following is not an importance of weed to a farmer (a) controls soil erosion (b) harbours crop diseases (c) source of animal feed (d) serves as cover crop','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',33),(34,'1.????? Weeds are difficult to control in the farm because (a) Their leaves are broader (b) Their seeds remain dormant for a long time in the soil (c) They have shallow root system (d) They help to control erosion','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',34),(35,'1.????? The weeds that complete their life cycle in more than two years are known as (a) Peculiar weeds (b) Annual weeds (c) Biennial weeds (d) Perennial weeds','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',35),(36,'1.?????  A method that involves the use of natural enemies or living organism to control weed                   is known as (a) Physical method (b) Chemical method (c) Biological method (d) Preventive method','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',36),(37,'1.????? Weeds are useful in the following ways EXCEPT A. provide food for livestock B. provide medicinal herbs C. supply of carbondioxide    D. provide fuel','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',37),(38,'1.????? The following are methods of controlling weeds EXCEPT A.  chemical B.medical      C.  mechanical     D.  biological','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',38),(39,'1.????? The chemical use to control weed is called (a) Pesticides (b) Rodenticides (c) Herbicides (d) Fungicides ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',39),(40,'1.????? The combination of two or more methods to combat weeds on the farm is termed A. Cultural control method   B. Integrated  controlmethod  C. Mechanical control method   D. Biological control method','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',40),(41,'1.????? The following are mechanical methods of weed control EXCEPT A. mowing B. hand pulling  C. use of living organisms D. use of cutlass','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',41),(42,'1.????? Weeds can be classified based on the following criteria EXCEPTA. food nutrient B. shape of leaves C. life span     D. habitat','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',42),(43,'1.????? The following are characteristics of weeds EXCEPTA. The seeds can remain dormant in the soil for a long time B. They are easily dispersed C. Seeds of weeds are highly viable D. they produce small quantity of pollen grains','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',43),(44,'1.????? Which of the following is NOT an importance of weed to man A.  Food    B. Herbs     C. Fuel     D. Work','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',44),(45,'1.????? The following are weeds that grow on other plants except A.Striga B.Dodder C. Mistletoe D.Terrestrial weeds.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',45),(46,'1.????? All forms of productive human efforts put into production is called A. capital B. land C. management D. labour','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',46),(47,'1.?????  Fixed capital or assets include all these EXCEPT A. Farm building B. Motor vehicle C. Farm tools D. Chemicals','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',47),(48,'1.?????  Organisms capable of causing damage either in the field or store are called A. Parasites B. Germs C. Pests D. Nematodes','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',48),(49,'1.????? All the following are  biting and chewing insect except A. Locust B. Aphid C. Cricket D. Termite ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',49),(50,'1.????? Which of the factors of production coordinates the other factors? A. land B. capital C. management D. labour','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',50),(51,'1.????? Biting and chewing insects likely attack which part  ofthe  plant A. Vegetative B. Fruit C. Root and tubers D. Flower','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',51),(52,'1.????? Organisms capable of causing damage either in the field or store are called A. Parasites B. Germs C. Pests D. Nematodes ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',52),(53,'1.????? The primary factor of production is A. Capital B. Land C. Labour D. Management.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',53),(54,'1.????? The reward of land as factor of production is A. Wages   B. Interest C. Profit D. Rent','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',54),(55,'1.????? The following are  factors of production except A. Land B. Labour C. Milling D. Capital','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',55),(56,'1.?????  Which factor of production has feeling? A. Land B. Labour C. Capital D. Asset','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',56),(57,'1.????? Human efforts put into production is termed as--. A. Entrepreneur   B. Labour C. Land D. Capital','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',57),(58,'1.????? Which of the following is regarded as a free gift of nature A.  Labour B. Capital C. Entrepreneur D. Land','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',58),(59,'1.????? The reward for labour is   A. Wages B. Rent C. Capital      D.  Interest  ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',59),(60,'1.?????  Which one among the following is the basic need of man A. food B.car C. handset D.money','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',60);
