INSERT INTO `basic7basictech3rdtermexquest900` VALUES (1,'1.Technology is developed in a society to provide all the following EXCEPT ----- (A) shelter (B) smuggling (C) food security (D) communication. ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',1),(2,'2.----- is NOT a technology-related career (A) Banking (B) computer programming \n(C) Architecture (D)Trade.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',2),(3,'3.Any profession which involves more thinking and knowing is ----- related A. artistic B. educational C. employment D. technology.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',3),(4,'4.The following are safety wears EXCEPT ------ (A) safety boots. (B) goggle (C) apron \n(D) wristwatch.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',4),(5,'5.Workshop can be defined as -----(A) where we can read (B) where we can do all practical jobs (C) where we can operate machines (D) where craftsmen can work.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',5),(6,'6.If water pipe linkage occurs in residential building, the best professional to be invited to repair it is ------- A. Panel beater B. Plumber C. Auto mechanic D. Carpenter.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',6),(7,'Fire -fighting equipment include all EXCEPT -------- (A) fire extinguisher (B) petrol (C) sand bucket (D) fire blanket','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',7),(8,'8.Shedding of  leaves is a property of ------ wood (A) soft (B) hard (C) pine (D) cedar','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',8),(9,'Woods are of ----- classes. (A) 2 (B) 3 (C) 4 (D) 5  ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',9),(10,'10.------ protects the growing part of the tree from the weather, animals and other injuries. A. Leaves B. Trunk B. Bark C. Root','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',10),(11,'Technology makes the world a global village through ------ (A) Electricity (B) Agriculture (C) Internet (D) Motorcycle. ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',11),(12,'12.All these are safety devices for motorist EXCEPT ------ (A) Helmets (B) seat belts (C) fire extinguisher (D) Caution triangle.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',12),(13,'13.----- is an example of non-ferrous metal(A) stainless (B) silver (C) cast iron (D) carbon steel.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',13),(14,'14.The high way code should be read and known by ------ (A) All road users (B) Pedestrians (C) Motorists (D) Cyclists.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',14),(15,'15.Margins are also called ???? (A) centre lines (B) border lines (C) middle lines (D) thick line ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',15),(16,'16.The quickest method by which the shape of an object can be communicated to others without using any drawing instrument except a pen or a pencil is (A) margin (B) middle lines (C) freehand sketching (D) pencil drawing ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',16),(17,'17.The following are techniques in freehand sketching EXCEPT (A)Sketching a Straight line (B)Sketching a curve (C)Sketching a Circle (D) lettering ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',17),(18,'18.The drawing instrument used for transferring measurement from the metric rule to the drawing sheet is called ???. (A) French curve (B) compass (C) scale rule (D) divider ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',18),(19,'19.Whatgives necessary information about the drawing such as name of designer, school, class, date, scale? (A) title block (B) lettering (C) thin lines (D) freehand sketch ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',19),(20,'20.The two styles of lettering are (A) verbal and reasoning (B) reasoning and vertical (C)vertical andinclined (D) incline and verbal ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',20),(21,'21.The shortest distance between two points is (A)incline line (B) uniform (C)straight line (D)short line ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',21),(22,'22.The following can be used for good board practice EXCEPT (A) T-square (B) Try square (C)pair of compasses (D)pair of dividers','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',22),(23,'23.The stock and blade of T-square form an angle ??.. (A)300 (B) 450 (C) 600 (D) 900','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',23),(24,'24.All these are parts of a tree EXCEPT (A) Root (B) Trunk or Stem (C) Branches (D) timber','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',24),(25,'25.We use ???. to protect the head in the workshop. (A) lab coat (B) Shoe (C) Helmet (D) Bucket ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',25),(26,'26.One of these is not an example of cutting tools? (a) Chisel (b) File (c) Hammer (d) Saw','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',26),(27,'27.Metals can be identified through their _______ (A) properties (B) ability (C) energy (D) power','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',27),(28,'28.All these are the properties of a ceramics EXCEPT ??.(A) They are brittle (B) They can easily be molded (C) They have high melting point (D) They are elastic in nature','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',28),(29,'29.????..is the processes (method) and products (materials) that make life easy and stress free.  (A) Technology (B) Science (C) Physics (D) Chemistry','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',29),(30,'30.A tool used for measuring length is _____. (a) Bradawl (b) caliper (c) plane (d) metric rule','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',30),(31,'31.A tool used to cut wood into two or more pieces in the workshop is called ___. (a) Saw (b) axe (c) file (d) scissors','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',31),(32,'32.One of these is not the unit used in measuring length of a material? (a) Centimeter (b) Millimeter (c) Kilograms (d) Meter','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',32),(33,'33.The following tools are used for holding jobs during cutting and chiseling on the bench except (a) Bench hook (b) Bench stop (c) Bench vice (d) hammer','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',33),(34,'34.Which of the following appliances cannot be fitted into a work bench?  (a) bench vice (b) bench hook (c) bench hammer (d) bench stop','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',34),(35,'35.A type of Hammer used for a general purposes work is called __. (a) Cross peen hammer (b) Straight peen hammer (c) Ball peen hammer (d) Planishing hammer','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',35),(36,'36.Which of the tools is used to fix nails into wooden materials?    (a) Hammer (b) Screwdriver (c) Plane (d) vice','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',36),(37,'37.The part of a drilling machine used to hold bits of various sizes is __________. (a) Plain (b) mallet (c) chuck (d) ratchet','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',37),(38,'38.Which of these instruments can be used to measure the diameter of the inner part of a pipe? (a) Divider (b) Outside caliper (c) Inside caliper (d) plier','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',38),(39,'39.Woodwork holding devices are the tools used to ______ on the workbench. (a) Hold work piece (b) cut work piece (c) mark work piece (d) hammer ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',39),(40,'Which of the following instruments is used for measuring angles? (a) 300, 600 set square (b) 450, 450 set square (c) Compass (d) protractor','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',40),(41,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1694220676.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 990px; height: 198px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;41.Identify the image shown below (a) Micrometer screw guage (b) Venier caliper (c) Odd? leg caliper (d) Inside caliper&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',41),(42,'Odd-leg caliper is also called ______________ (a) Outside caliper (b) Internal caliper (c) Jenny?s caliper (d) Venier calipe','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',42),(43,'43.The following are cutting and pairing tools EXCEPT __________. (a) bench hook (b) chisel (c) jack plane (d) Spoke shave','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',43),(44,'44.________ are used to obtain a good, smooth surface and correct size required. (a) Saws (b) rulers (c) planes (d) G-Clamps','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',44),(45,'45.The tool used for taking out nails in wood work is called _______. (a) Gauge (b) pincers (c) chisels (d) pliers','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',45),(46,'Which of the following is a driving tool? (a)center punch (b) chisel (c) file (d) screw driver   ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',46),(47,'47.An activity carried out to get a machine in good working condition is known as ______.   (a) greasing (b) oiling (c) maintenance (d) sharpening','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',47),(48,'48.Which of these maintenance practices is NOT preventive?     (a) checking oil gauge level  (b) checking acid water level (c) replacement of fuse in the fuse box (d) inspection of bolts and nuts of a car tyre','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',48),(49,'.Which of the following tool is used for marking drill points? (a) Scriber (b) Dot punch \n(c) Pencil (d) Hammer ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',49),(50,'50.The  tool for making-out large diameter where compass cannot be use is called (a) Trammel (b) Hack saw (c) miter square (d) chisel','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',50),(51,'51.Accurate markings that are horizontal or vertical are possible only with the use of the _______.  (a) hammer (b) protractor (c) surface plate (d) surface gauge   ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',51),(52,'52.The Maintenance that aims at restoring a broken equipment to its original operating condition is _____ maintenance. (a) Preventive (b) corrective (c) predictive (d) daily ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',52),(53,'53. Metals can be prevented from rusting by _____________. (a) applying water to them   (b) applying acid on them (c) rubbing oil on them (d) removing grease from them ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',53),(54,'54. Dot punching is a method in _____. (a) measuring (b) cutting (c) boring (d) marking-out','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',54),(55,'55.Mallets are _______ hammers.  (a) hard (b) soft-face (c) glass (d) metallic ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',55),(56,'.56. Checking the level of engine oil in a vehicle is a type of _____ maintenance.\n(a) corrective (b) preventive (c) replacement (d) predictive','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',56),(57,'57. Which of these tools is not a driving tool? (a) Hammer (b) mallet (c) screwdriver \n(d) bench vice','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',57),(58,'58. Which of these is not a method of caring for files?\nA.Store in the rack, separated from each other B. Use old files only on hardened steel C.  Do not rub files together D. Use a file card to clean after clogging','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',58),(59,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/421561440.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 948px; height: 157px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;59.The diagram below is called ______. (a) Flat screw driver (b) Punch (c) Scriber (d) Chisel&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',59),(60,'60.A metal tool used for tightening and loosing nuts and bolts is ______.  (a) screw driver (b) spanner (c) drill bit (d) chisel','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',60);
