ock (a) white (b) red (c) black (d) purple','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',16),(17,'?The ?? is referred to as the ultimate source of energy (a) sun (b) food (c) water (d) light','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',17),(18,'?Energy possessed by a body in motion is (a) potential (b) chemical (c) nuclear (d) kinetic','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',18),(19,'?Energy possessed by a body at rest is (a) potential (b) chemical (c) nuclear (d) kinetic','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',19),(20,'?Light travels at about ??.km/s In a straight line (a) 400,000 (b) 200,000 (c) 300,000 (d) 500,000','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',20),(21,'The energy produced when the nucleus of an atom is splitted is (a) potential (b) chemical (c) nuclear (d) kinetic','A','B','C','D','','C',0,'',21),(22,'?Which of the following metals exists in liquid state (a) Iron (b) Mercury (c) Gold (d) Copper','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',22),(23,'Transition from solid to gaseous state is called (a) Condensation (b) Freezing (c) Sublimation (d) Evaporation','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',23),(24,'?Transition from liquid to solid state is called (a) Condensation (b) Freezing (c) Sublimation (d) Evaporation','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',24),(25,'?Transition from liquid to gaseous state is called (a) Condensation (b) Freezing (c) Sublimation (d) Evaporation','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',25),(26,'?Matter is made up of small particles called (a) atom (b) substance (c) molecules (d) chemicals','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',26),(27,'The basic unit of life is called (a) tissue (b) cell (c) organ (d) system','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',27),(28,'Plants removes carbon-dioxide from the atmosphere during (a) photosynthesis (b) respiration (c) excretion (d) reproduction','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',28),(29,'The process through which green plants manufacture their food in the presence of sunlight and chlorophyll is called (a) photosynthesis (b) respiration (c) excretion (d) reproduction','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',29),(30,'.???? is a change in position of an organism (a) respiration (b) locomotion (c) excretion (d) growth','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',30),(31,'The moon revolves round the earth in about ------- days (a) 14 (b) 21 (c) 29 (d) 365','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',31),(32,'?There are ____ planets in the universe (a) 7 (b) 8 (c) 9 (d) 10','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',32),(33,'The first planets in the solar system from the sun is -------(a) mars (b) mercury (c) earth (d) Saturn','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',33),(34,'The solar system comprises of ------ (a) the sun and planets (b) the sun and earth (c) the sun and Jupiter (d) earth and mars','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',34),(35,'?Rotation is the movement of the earth round its ----- (a)Plane (b) Surface (c) Axis (d)Arc','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',35),(36,'The earth complete one rotation in -- hours (a) 32 (b) 12 (c) 72 (d) 24','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',36),(37,'?The earth carry out--- type of movement (a) 3 (b) 2 (c) 4 (d) 5','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',37),(38,'The rotation of the earth around its axis causes (a) sunshine (b) night (c) day and night (d) rainfall','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',38),(39,'?An astronaut first went into space in (a) 1960 (b) 1961 (c) 1962 (d) 1963','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',39),(40,'?An astronaut landed on the moon in (a) 1967 (b) 1966 (c)1969 (d) 1965','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',40),(41,'?There are ?.. phases during the rotation of the moon (a) 3 (b) 4 (c) 5 (d) 6','A','B','C','D','','5',0.5,'',41),(42,'?Revolution of the earth causes (a) season (b) night (c) day and night (d) sunshine','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',42),(43,'?Which of the following planet has no moon (a) Venus (b) Jupiter (c) Saturn (d) Neptune','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',43),(44,'?A quantity with both magnitude and direction is said to be (a) Scalar (b) Matter (c) Vector (d) Mass','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',44),(45,'The weight of an object in the moon is ??.. of the weight of the object on earth (a)1/2 (b) ? (c) 1/6 (d) 1/8','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',45),(46,'?If an astronaut weighs 54N on earth, in the moon he/she will weigh (a) 7 (b) 8 (c) 9 (d)10','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',46),(47,'The unit of weight is (a) Seconds (b) Newton (c) kilogram (d) metre','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',47),(48,'?The inner part of the solar system includes (a) Saturn (b) Venus (c) Jupiter (d) Uranus','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',48),(49,'the first Astronaut in space was (a) Neil Armstrong (b) Yuri Gagarin (c) Thomas Edison (d) Marie Currie','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',49),(50,'Neil Armstrong was an astronaut from (a) Russia (b) America (c) South Africa (d) China','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',50),(51,'???. Causes motion (a) energy (b) time (c) force (d) temperature','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',51),(52,'In which of the force is the direction towards the earth? (a) gravitational (b) electrical (c) magnetic (d) frictional','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',52),(53,'?In which of the force is the direction from the north pole to the south pole? (a) gravitational (b) electrical (c) magnetic (d) frictional','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',53),(54,'?In which of the force is the direction from positive to negative charge? (a) gravitational (b) electrical (c) magnetic (d) frictional','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',54),(55,'The following are examples of non-contact force except (a) magnetic force (b) frictional (c) electrical (d) gravitational','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',55),(56,'What is the work done by a man who lifts a block of 30kg through a height of 3 meters? (g=10m/s2 ) (a) 90J (b) 100J (c) 900J (d) 1000J','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',56),(57,'Balanced forces are  (a) always causing a change in direction (b) in a state of equilibrium (c) not opposite in direction (d) not equal in size','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',57),(58,'?Unlike charges ??? each other (a) repel (b) collides (c) attract (d) absorb','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',58),(59,'?A boy is pushing a box across the floor. If he applies a force of 20N and the box accelerates at 2m/s2, what is the mass of the box? (a) 10N (b) 10kg (c) 10J (d) 40N','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',59),(60,'The force responsible for a stone falling towards the ground is a ?? force (a) magnetic force (b) frictional (c) electrical (d) gravitational','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',60),(61,' ','','','','','','',0,'',0);
