INSERT INTO `basic8basictech3rdtecat1quest641` VALUES (1,'1.What is a gear used for? A. Making juice B. Transmitting motion between shafts  C. Blowing air D. Playing music.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',1),(2,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1740317018.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 883px; height: 177px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;2.The arrangement of the gears below is known as ? A. Gear box B. Gear unit C. Gear train D. Gear loop.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',2),(3,'3.What must be done to prevent wearing of gears? A. Paint them B. Hit them with a hammer C. Lubricate them regularly  D. Wash them with water.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',3),(4,'4.When gears are not properly meshed? A. They move faster B. They produce more power C. They can get damaged or stop moving   D. They become smoother.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',4),(5,'The gear that receives power from the engine is called? A. Idler gear B. Driver gear  C. Driven gear D. Starter gear','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',5),(6,'Which is the function of the idler gear? A. It makes noise B. It keeps the gear train clean C. It helps the driver and driven gears move in the same direction  D. It slows down the machine','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',6),(7,'7.A type of gear that has teeth that are straight and parallel to the shaft is?  A. Helical gear  B. Spur gear C. Worm gear  D. Bevel gear.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',7),(8,'&lt;p&gt;What type of gear is shown in the figure below? A. Rack and pinion B. Worm gear C. Bevel gear D. Spur gear.&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1215258409.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 925px; height: 253px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',8),(9,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1526254016.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 925px; height: 253px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;9.The part labelled A is the is the? A. Rack B. pinion C. base D. head.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',9),(10,'The part labelled B is the is the? A. Rack B. pinion  C. base  D. head','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',10),(11,'11.The tiny thread-like units that make up wood called? A. Cells B. Roots C. Fibers  D. Branches.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',11),(12,'12.The two main types of wood? A. Strong wood and weak wood B. Light wood and dark wood C. Hardwood and softwood  D. Old wood and new wood.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',12),(13,'13.Which type of tree gives us hardwood? A. Coniferous trees B. Deciduous trees  C. Tropical trees D. Evergreen trees.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',13),(14,'14.Which of the following is an example of softwood? A. Mahogany B. Sapele C. Cedar  D. Opepe','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',14),(15,'15.The type of tree growth that makes the tree grow taller? A. Secondary growth B. Horizontal growth C. Primary growth D. Side growth.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',15),(16,'16.Which of these is the correct order of wood processing? A. Cutting ? Painting ? Seasoning ? Washing B. Felling ? Conversion ? Seasoning ? Preservation C. Harvesting ? Burning ? Drying ? Storing D. Felling ? Selling ? Transporting ? Packaging.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',16),(17,'17.You are making a knife blade that must stay sharp even when hot. Which alloy steel is best? A. High speed steel  B. Stainless steel C. Mild steel D. Wrought iron.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',17),(18,'18.Which of the following metals is most likely to be used in kitchen utensils because it resists rust? A. Cast iron B. Stainless steel  C. Mild steel D. Pig iron','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',18),(19,'19.A student is shown three samples of metal: one is magnetic, one is shiny and non-magnetic, and one is soft. Which is the non-ferrous metal? A. Steel B. Wrought iron C. Aluminum  D. Cast iron.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',19),(20,'20.If you need to remove impurities from iron ore using heat, which process would you perform? A. Forging B. Casting C. Smelting  D. Welding.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',20);
