INSERT INTO `basic8basictech3rdtermexquest336` VALUES (1,'The first emergency treatment given to a sick or injured person before taking him to the doctor is called.  A. first Aid B. quck action C. rushing D. service to humanity','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',1),(2,'2.The most aspect of first aid treatment is ?? A. stop bleeding B. life saving C. restore further injuries D. predictions','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',2),(3,'3.Which of the following is NOT a trauma injury? A. electrocution B. drowning C. fever D. fracture. ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',3),(4,'One of these is not an instrument commonly found in a first aid box  A. syringe B. scissors C. forceps D. thermometer. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',4),(5,'Rescue operations begin with A. adequate training B. adequate information C. selection of instruments and equipment. D. Securing the environment. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',5),(6,'6.The letter B in the ABC of first aid could stand for all of the following except A. breathing B. breeding C. bleeding D. breaks','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',6),(7,'7.The following are safety wears EXCEPT A. apron B. cover shoe C. hand gloves D. wrist watch','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',7),(8,'8.Which of the following materials is NOT used in making ceramics? A. Lime A. Clay C. Cement D. Mud','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',8),(9,'9. A straight line drawn through the center of a circle and meeting the circumference at both ends is known as ??.. A. radius B. diameter C. normal D. chord','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',9),(10,'10.Which of the following causes accident in the workshop? A. Cleanliness A. use of safety devices C. fatigue D. following safety habits.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',10),(11,'11.A quadrilateral is a plane figure bounded by  ??.. sides.  A. five B. four    C. two  D. three.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',11),(12,'.A polygon with twelve sides is known as A. pentagon  B. undecagon C. dodecagon D. nonagon','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',12),(13,'13.A perpendicular line is always at ??? to the horizontal line.  A. 300      B. 450     C. 900 D. 600','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',13),(14,'14.The property of a material that makes it stretch and return to its original size when force is applied on it is ??? A. ductility B. magnetic C. fusibility D. elasticity.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',14),(15,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/831849795.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 933px; height: 220px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;15.The angle represented in fig. 1 is A. acute B. right angle C. obtuse D. reflex&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',15),(16,'16.The circles in fig. 2 are A. essentric B. concentric C. normal D. round.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',16),(17,'17.Another name for enlargement is ??? A. transfusion B. reduction C. scale mapping D. transformation.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',17),(18,'18.Which of the following is a regular polygon with seven sides A. heptagon B. decagon C. pentagon D. hexagon.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',18),(19,'19.Machine tools powered by electric motors that can be easily carried when working on work piece is called A. power machine B. portable machine C. stationary machine D. heavy machine.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',19),(20,'20.What sawing method is used for conversion the engineering material in fig. 3? A. tangential B. plain C. quarter D. normal','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',20),(21,'21.A liquid substance which has power of bonding two or more materials together is ?.. A. Abrasive B. Hinges C. Adhesive D. Acid.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',21),(22,'22.One of the following is NOT a type of hinges A. Tee hinges B. Flat hinges C. Butt hinge D. Global hinges.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',22),(23,'The product of two lengths is usually known as ??. A. breath B. volume C. area D. distance ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',23),(24,'24.Paper and pulp are obtained  from one of the following engineering materials A. plastics A. ceramics C.wood D. metals','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',24),(25,'25.Which of the following is not a product of ceramic? A. chair B. pots C. statues D. tiles','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',25),(26,'26.Terminals and plates of batteries are made up of ?? A. copper B. lead C. silver D. zinc','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',26),(27,'27.Some metals are ferrous because they contain ???.. A. Aluminum B. iron C. steel D. elements','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',27),(28,'28.The body of an aircraft is made out of ?? A. aluminum B. bronze C. copper D. gold','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',28),(29,'29.The alloy of copper and zinc is ??. A. silver B. Brass C. Bronze D. Duralumin','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',29),(30,'A thin sheet of wood used in furniture is called ??.. A. plywood B. veneer C. chipboard D. particle board','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',30),(31,'31.Rubber can be used in manufacturing of the following materials EXCEPT A. hose B. shoes C. tyres D. handle of cooking pots','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',31),(32,'32.Metal that break easily when struck are said to be A. elastic B. brittle C. tough D. malleable','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',32),(33,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/384592384.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 892px; height: 253px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The power machine shown above is called ??. A. Jig saw B. cut-class saw C. chain saw D. jig saw.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',33),(34,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1453932285.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 892px; height: 253px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;34.The saw in fig. 4 is used for ---- A. conversion B. seasoning C. planning D. thicknessing.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',34),(35,'35.Which document contains the rules and regulations guiding the operation of machines?   A. Manufacturer?s instruction  B. Retailers  C. Standard organisation D. Government.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',35),(36,'36.Which of these is a distinguishable property of rubber? A. Malleability B. Elasticity C.Toughness D. Ductility.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',36),(37,'37.Which of the following parts protects a growing tree from harm?   A. leaves  B. branches C. bark D. trunk.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',37),(38,'1.?The area where Tariff is paid is ?? A. forest reserve B. free area C. market D. saw-mill.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',38),(39,'All these are the advantages of manufactured board, EXCEPT,  A. They are available in flat large sheets. B. They can be cut easily and worked on. C.They can be easily nailed without splitting.  D. They are too hard to work upon.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',39),(40,'Which of these is NOT a reason for seasoning wood?    A. for durability   B. for more weight   C. to reduce weight   D.  to minimize bacteria attack   ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',40),(41,'41.What is the percentage moisture content of wood which weighs 60kg before and 40kg after seasoning?   A.  75%   B.  50%   C.  33%   D.  20%   ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',41),(42,'42.The process of separating a metal from its ore is called  ??.  A. casting B. dressing  C. smelting D. separation.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',42),(43,'43.Blast furnace is used for processing ??.. A.  Pig iron   B. wrought iron   C.  stainless  D.  cast iron.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',43),(44,'44.What part of the tree helps in secondary (horizontal) growth?  A. Bark B. Root C. Cambium D. Leaf.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',44),(45,'45.The money paid to cut down trees in the Free Area is called?  A. O.T.V  B. License C. Tariff  D. Ticket.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',45),(46,'46.What does it mean when a preservative is toxic? A. It makes the wood smell nice B. It keeps the wood warm C. It kills insects and fungi that destroy wood D. It turns the wood into plastic.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',46),(47,'47.Penetration is an important property of a timber preservative because?  A. it makes the wood change color B. it can enter deep into the wood to protect it from inside  C. it keeps the wood soft  D. it makes the wood slippery.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',47),(48,'48.What does cost-effective mean when choosing a timber preservative? A. It is very expensive B. It comes from the forest C. It is cheap and easy to get D. It grows on wood.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',48),(49,'49.The main purpose of applying wood preservatives is?  A. To change the wood\'s color B. To make the wood heavier C. To protect wood from insects and fungi D. To decorate the wood.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',49),(50,'50.What are wood preservatives made to poison? A. Paint and polish B. Destructive agents like termites  C. Tree roots D. Tree leaves.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',50),(51,'1.?Which of the following is a method of applying wood preservatives? A. Rolling B. Stirring C. Brushing D. Bending.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',51),(52,'52.What is perspective drawing? A. Drawing with crayons B. Drawing things as they appear smaller when far away C. Drawing only flat shapes  D. Drawing with only black pencils','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',52),(53,'53.Which type of oblique has its receding sides drawn half full size?  A. Cavalier B. cabinet C. orthographic  D. perspective','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',53),(54,'54.Which of the pictorial drawing shows the representation of the apparent reduction in size of a distant object? A. isometric  B. orthographic  C. perspective  D. oblique.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',54),(55,'55.In isometric projection, receding lines are drawn at  ??? degrees to the horizontal lines.  A.  15    B. 30 C. 45 D. 60','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',55),(56,'56.One of these is not a pictorial drawing. A. orthographic projection B. isometric projection C. oblique projection D. perspective projection.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',56),(57,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1754079250.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 1008px; height: 463px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;57.The diagram in fig.5 is a/an ?.. drawing A. isometric B. Oblique C. orthographic D. perspective.&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',57),(58,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1542346814.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 1008px; height: 463px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;58.Points VP1 and VP2 are called A. vanishing points B. lines of sight C. horizon line D. ground line&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',58),(59,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1241897380.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 1008px; height: 463px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;59.The number of perspective points in the diagram are A. 1 B. 2 C 3 D. 4&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',59),(60,'60.How many vanishing points are used in one-point perspective drawing? A. One B. Two C. Three D. None.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',60);
