INSERT INTO `biolss1cat2quest387` VALUES (1,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of the following is NOT a characteristic of freshwater habitat? A. Low salinity B. High density C. Varying temperature D. Shallow depth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(2,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Examples of stagnant freshwater habitats include all except A. Lake B. Pond C. Stream D. puddle&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(3,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;What structure helps water snails attach to surfaces in freshwater? A. Tail fin B. Cilia C. Foot D. Gills&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(4,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of the following is a floating plant in freshwater habitats? A. Ceratophyllum B. Duckweed C. Hornwort D. Bacteria&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(5,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which adaptation enables plankton to float in freshwater habitats? A. Sharp claws B. Heavy shells C. Oil globules D. Long legs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(6,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;The zone in freshwater where light penetration is greatest is called the A. benthic zone B. aphotic zone C. dark zone D. photic zone&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(7,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;A farmer notices that fish in his shallow pond survive dry seasons better than those in a nearby stream. The likely reason is that the pond fish A. are smaller B. swim faster C. can burrow into the mud D. drink more water&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(8,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Marsh habitats are known for having  A. dry soil and deep roots B. oxygen-rich soil C. waterlogged, anaerobic soil D. thick forest canopy&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(9,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of the following is an animal typically found in a marsh habitat? A. Camel B. Heron C. Lizard D. Parrot&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;AB&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(10,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of these is NOT a type of marsh?  A. Salt marsh B. Freshwater marsh C. Desert marsh D. Inland marsh&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(11,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Marshes help purify water by A. trapping rain B. blocking waves C. filtering pollutants D. storing minerals&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(12,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;The tropical rainforest has trees thatA. shed their leaves every month B. have narrow leavesC. grow only in dry season D. form a canopy in layers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(13,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;In a forest, a monkey leaps between trees while avoiding predators. This is an example of adaptation for A. Gliding B. Camouflage C. Jumping D. migration&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(14,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of the following is characteristic of arid land? A. High rainfall B. Thick vegetation C. High evaporation D. Cold temperature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(15,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;A plant that thrives in desert conditions is likely to have A. broad flat leaves B. hairy roots C. thick waxy stems D. soft fleshy fruits&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(16,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;A biology student observes a paramecium dividing into two daughter cells. This process is A. Budding B. binary fission C. multiple fission D. conjugation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(17,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Multiple fission differs from binary fission in that it A. forms one new cell B. involves sexual reproduction C. produces many daughter cells at once D. happens only in multicellular organisms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(18,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;Which of the following is an application of asexual reproduction in agriculture?&lt;br /&gt;\nA. Breeding cattle B. Pollinating flowers C. Vegetative propagation D. Cross-pollination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(19,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;In conjugation, genetic material is exchanged between&lt;br /&gt;\nA. parent and offspring B. two similar cells C. plant and animal D. two different species&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(20,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;,serif&quot;&gt;A teacher gives her students four pictures: Amoeba, Paramecium, Spirogyra, and Earthworm. Which of these reproduces only sexually? A. Amoeba B. Paramecium C. Spirogyra D. Earthworm&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0);
