INSERT INTO `civicca2quest316` VALUES (1,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;What is the primary purpose of a constitution in a country? a) To enforce strict laws b) To establish a monarchy c) To outline a system of governance d) To encourage political conflicts &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(2,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which part of a constitution typically guarantees the fundamental rights of citizens? a) Preamble b) Executive Branch c) Legislative Branch d) Bill of Rights &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(3,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;. The process of amending a constitution involves: a) Rewriting the entire constitution b) Creating a new branch of government c) Adding new articles to the constitution d) Appointing new constitutional experts &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(4,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;What does the doctrine of separation of powers entail in a constitution? a) Merging all powers in a single branch of government b) Dividing powers between the government and the military c) Distributing powers among different branches of government d) Allowing foreign powers to influence domestic affairs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(5,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;5. Which type of constitution is unwritten and evolves over time based on customs and conventions? a) Codified constitution b) Authoritarian constitution c) Unilateral constitution d) Uncodified constitution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(6,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The written documents that explicitly outline the fundamental laws and principles of a country&amp;#39;s governance are known as: a) Traditional sources b) Philosophical sources c) Statutory sources d) Enacted sources &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(7,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;. Which of the following is an example of an unwritten source of a constitution? a) Legal statutes b) Historical documents c) International treaties d) Custom and tradition &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(8,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;&amp;hellip;..contains the right and duties of the country&amp;rsquo;s leaders and citizens. a) constitution b) Statutory c) Judicial d) Enacted book &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(9,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;When international treaties and agreements shape a country&amp;#39;s domestic laws and rights, they serve as: a) Constitutional precedents b) International principles c) Conventional sources d) External sources &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(10,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The scope of a constitution includes: a) The basic rights of citizens b) The distribution of powers within government c) Traditional cultural practices d) International trade agreements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(11,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which of the following cannot be found in a constitution? (a) fundamental human right (b) manifestoes of political parties (c) organs of government (d) duties and obligations of citizens.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(12,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;12. Which of the following is not a source of a country&amp;rsquo;s constitution? (a) Legislative decisions (b) Past constitutions (c) Writ of Mandamus (d) Judicial Precedents&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(13,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;13. Which of the following is not within the scope of a constitution? (a) Fundamental Human Right (b) Organs of government (c) Coup d&amp;rsquo;etat (d) Preamble&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(14,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;14. A constitution is the (a) written document of traditional practices (b) functional aspect of government activities (c) supreme document of the government (d) fundamental laws of the land. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(15,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;15. A constitution is important because it (a) teaches moral values of the society (b) prescribes rules for those who govern (c) serves as source of conflicts in society (d) describes the law and admonishes obedience&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(16,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;16. The Macpherson Constitution of 1951 was notable for its introduction of ____________. a) Regional governments b) One-party system c) Military rule d) Absolute monarchy &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(17,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;17. A rigid constitution is a feature of (a) unitary system (b) monarchical system (c) federal system (d) confederal system. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(18,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;18.The Macpherson Constitution of 1951 granted more powers to the ____________. a) Colonial administrators b) Traditional rulers c) Federal government d) Local councils&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(21,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Calibri&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;19. Which of the following is not a main source of a constitution? (a) Judicial precedents (b) Legislative decisions (c) Previous constitution (d) Public deliberations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(22,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0in; margin-right:0in&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;20. A constitution whose procedure for amendment is the same as that of making an ordinary law is referred to as (a) a unitary constitution (b) an unwritten constitution (c) a flexible constitution (d) a confederal constitution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0);
