INSERT INTO `civss1cat23rdtermquest791` VALUES (1,'1. When laws are not enforced in the society,it leads A.anarchy B. endurance C. peace D. progress','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',1),(2,'2. The following are some of the reasons some students join cult in school except A. Search for security B. Success in marriage C. Success in academics D. Search for political identity','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',2),(3,'3. The following are the consequences of cultism except A. C.Timely graduation  B.Untimely death C.Health problems D. Lack of peace','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',3),(4,'4. The act of doing the right thing at the right time and at the right place is called A. honesty B. justice  C. orderliness  D. integrity','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',4),(5,'5. Which of the following activities is associated with cultists? A. Decent dressing  B. Espionage in intelligence  C. Meeting at godly hours D.violence and vandalism ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',5),(6,'6. The word for lawless society is  A. anarchy  B. apathy  C.orderliness  D. obsession','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',6),(7,'7. The effect of queuing up in public places is A. orderliness B. transparency C. honesty D. humility ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',7),(8,'8. The father of pyrate confraternity in Nigeria is. A.Chinua Achebe  B.Herbert Macaulay  C.Olusegun Obasanjo D.Wole Soyinka','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',8),(9,'9. One of the following is a manifestation of disorderliness in the society. A. Patience B. Patriotism  C. Strife D. Sacrifice','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',9),(10,'10. The following are all preventive measures against cultism except A. campaign against cultism B. injustice   C. adequate parental care D. abiding in rules and regulation of the country','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',10),(11,'11. Attempting to jump the queue is a bad habit that causes A. orderliness B. disorderliness C. propriety  D. pious','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',11),(12,'12. The Universal Declaration of Human Rights was officially ratified in the year A.1914 B.1948 C.1960 D. 1966','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',12),(13,'13. Constituted authority is necessary in the society because it A. promotes international relation B. ensures security of lives and properties C. serves as an agent of socialization D. provide scholarship for higher education ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',13),(14,'14. Law breakers are known  as  A. deviants  B. bad Citizens  C. conformist  D.  Law haters ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',14),(15,'15. One of the following does not encourage orderliness at the group level. A. Impatience B. tolerance C. queuing culture  D. environmental sanitation','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',15),(16,'16. If Laws enacted are not enforced in a society, there is likely to be A. peace B.  enemies C. anarchy  D. security ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',16),(17,'17. The major role of the Police is to A. punish law breakers   B. arrest law breakers  C. ensure that people obey enacted laws  D. prosecute law breakers. ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',17),(18,'18. Orderliness can be observed in the following places except A. Family B. School C. Church D. Graveyard ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',18),(19,'19. Orderliness as a virtue and value rest in the following qualities except A. Strife B. Patience C. Love and patriotism D. Sacrifice ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',19),(20,'20. Oderliness can play the various roles in the items listed below except A. Serving as a yardstick for assessing actions and behaviour B. Training the mind to accept social values C. Ensuring peace D. Discouraging co-operation ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',20);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `civss1cat23rdtermquest791` ENABLE KEYS */;
