rd “constant” can best be replaced by ______','changing','faithful','regular','permanent','reliable','D',1,'',75),(78,'A person who takes care of animals is called a ______','veterinary','zoologist','shepherd','vet doctor','pastor','D',1,'',76),(79,'What is the noun form of the verb “depart”?','departure','departed','departing','departance','departion','A',1,'',77),(80,'The superlative form of “bad” is ______','worse','worser','more bad','worst','baddest','D',1,'',78),(81,'The word “rare” means ______','scarce','common','frequent','regular','usual','A',1,'',79),(82,'“The child is asleep.” The negative form is:','The child is not sleep','The child is not sleeping','The child is not asleep','The child does not sleep','The child is wake','C',1,'',80),(83,'Which of the following words is the odd one out?','cow','goat','horse','lion','sheep','D',1,'',81),(84,'The plural of “foot” is ______','foots','footes','feets','feet','D','D',1,'',82),(85,'“We saw them playing.” The underlined word is a/an ______','noun','verb','adjective','adverb','pronoun','B',1,'',83),(86,'Choose the correct sentence.','He go to school everyday.','He goes to school every day.','He going to school every day.','He goed to school every day.','He gone to school every day.','B',1,'',84),(87,'Which of the following is not a vowel?','a','e','i','r','u','D',1,'',85),(88,'The comparative form of “good” is ______','gooder','more good','better','best','very good','C',1,'',86),(89,'“Tunde runs faster than me.” The word “faster” is a ______','noun','adjective','verb','adverb','pronoun','D',1,'',87),(90,'Which of these is a question tag? “You are coming, ______?”','will you','won’t you','aren’t you','do you','did you','C',1,'',88),(91,'Which of the following sentences is correct?','The childrens are playing.','The children is playing.','The child are playing.','The children are playing.','Childrens is playing.','D',1,'',89),(92,'“He works hard.” Choose the correct question form:','Do he work hard?','Does he works hard?','Does he work hard?','Do he works hard?','Is he works hard?','C',1,'',90),(93,'What is the meaning of the word “frequently”?','always','rarely','sometimes','often','never','D',1,'',91),(94,'“The book was interesting.” What is the opposite of “interesting”?','boring','exciting','amusing','educative','funny','A',1,'',92),(95,'“They have gone to the market.” Change to past tense.','They go to the market.','They went to the market.','They gone to the market.','They going to the market.','They goes to the market.','B',1,'',93),(96,'Choose the word that means the same as “enormous”.','tiny','small','huge','little','few','C',1,'',94),(97,'Which word is correctly spelt?','buisness','busines','business','buziness','bisiness','C',1,'',95),(98,'“She sings better than her sister.” The underlined word is a ______','verb','noun','conjunction','pronoun','adjective','A',1,'',96),(99,'Which of these is an interjection?','Quickly','Beautiful','Wow','And','Behind','C',1,'',97),(100,'What part of speech is the word “under”?','noun','verb','adverb','preposition','adjective','D',1,'',98),(101,'“The boy that won the prize is my cousin.” The underlined clause is a ______','main clause','dependent clause','relative clause','noun clause','adverbial clause','C',1,'',99),(102,'Which of the following is a punctuation mark?','capital','bracket','letter','comma','symbol','D',1,'',100);
