INSERT INTO `econss2cat23rdtermquest23` VALUES (1,'Deflation means ------ a) A rise in the general price level b) A decrease in the general price level c) An increase in the money supply d) A decrease in the money supply','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',1),(2,'Which of the following can contribute to deflation? a) Increased consumer spending b) High demand for goods and services c) Rapidly growing economy d) Decreased consumer spending ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',2),(3,'3. Falling housing prices, decreasing wages, and lower consumer spending are characteristics of:  a) Inflation b) Hyperinflation c) Deflation d) Stagflation Question ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',3),(4,'4. A continuous fall in the general price level is called A recession B depression C Stagflation D Deflation','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',4),(5,'5. What is a potential cause of deflation during an economic downturn? a) High levels of consumer spending b) Excessive government borrowing c) Rapid growth in the money supply d) Decreased aggregate demand ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',5),(6,'Which of the following is an example of demand-deflation? a) Increased government spending on infrastructure b) Rise in consumer spending due to tax cuts c) Reduced consumer spending leading to lower prices d) Central bank reducing interest rates ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',6),(7,'7. What is industrialization? a) A process of turning natural resources into consumer goods b) The transition from an agrarian-based economy to one centered around manufacturing and industry c) The advancement of rural lifestyles over urban ones d) The promotion of traditional handicrafts over mechanized production ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',7),(8,'8. Which of the following is a primary driver of industrialization? a) Agriculture b) Barter system c) Subsistence economy d) Technological innovation ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',8),(9,'9. Industrialization often leads to: a) Increased dependence on agriculture. b) Urbanization and the growth of cities. c) Preservation of traditional craftsmanship. d) A decline in technological advancements. ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',9),(10,'10. Which sector of the economy experiences the most significant growth during industrialization? a) Primary sector b) Secondary sector c) Tertiary sector d) Quaternary sector ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',10),(11,'11. The Industrial Revolution, a major period of industrialization, began in: a) The 15th century b) The 18th century c) The 19th century d) The 20th century ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',11),(12,'12. Which of the following is a potential negative consequence of rapid industrialization? a) Increased economic stability b) Environmental pollution c) Reduced unemployment rates d) Preservation of traditional cultures ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',12),(13,'Where was oil first discovered in commercial quantities in Nigeria? Oloibiri  b.  Warri  c.  EleseEleme d. Onitsha','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',13),(14,'Crude oil was first discovered in Nigeria in A. 2007 B. 1907 C. 1908 D. 1936','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',14),(15,'15. The following depict positive contributions of Petroleum to Nigerian economy except A. Mono-product economy B. Employment opportunities C. Man-power development D. Increase in GDP','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',15),(16,'16. Which of these is not a function of OPEC A. to ensure efficient and regular supply of oil to the world market B.?  to maintain relatively stable price of petroleum C. to redistribute income among member states \n            D. protection of the economic interest of member states \n','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',16),(17,'Which of the following is not a founding member of OPEC? a) Saudi Arabia b) Iran c) Kuwait d) Russia ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',17),(18,'How does OPEC influence global oil prices? a) By setting fixed prices for oil exports b) By manipulating oil supply to balance demand and prices c) By subsidizing oil production costs for member countries d) By encouraging member countries to produce more oil than they need','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',18),(19,'19. In order to stabilize oil price in the world market, there is the need for OPEC members to (a) always have budget deficit (b) encourage competition among one another (c) fix the price of oil related products (d) adhere to production quotas','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',19),(20,'20. What is the main goal of OPEC? a) Promoting renewable energy sources b) Controlling global oil prices c) Maximizing oil production at any cost d) Ensuring stable income for its member countries through coordination of oil production\n\n','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',20);
