INSERT INTO `engb83rd2025quest339` VALUES (1,'Read the passage below carefully and answer questions 1-5.\nA few minutes before the football encounter between Enyimba Football Club and the Yankari Football Club was going to begin, all the gates to the Jokolo Stadium were shut. The stadium had already been jam-packed but many people were still outside the stadium. These people could not get in because they had no tickets.\nJust then a small boy began to push his way between the legs of the crowd. He was almost trampled upon by the crowd as many people were suffocated. At last, the boy managed to reach the gate, put his hand in his pocket and pulled out a ticket. He asked the gateman to open the gate. The man first looked at him and asked, \'Where is your ticket, you think you can use your stature to enter without ticket?\' The boy then showed him his ticket. The gateman looked at the ticket to make sure that it was not fake. \'It is genuine, my father bought it for me long ago\', the boy cried at the top of his voice.\n\'Did you come by yourself? Your father likes watching football, doesn\'t he?\' the gateman asked the boy. \'Oh yes, he does very much\' said the boy. \'Then why didn\'t he come with you?\' \'Oh, he\'s still at home looking for his ticket\', replied the boy. The boy had hardly finished answering the question when there were shouts of, \'A goal\' from the inside of the stadium. The boy was then allowed in. As the boy got in, another boy, Ayo, who was also a football fan wanted to follow him but had no ticket, so he was disallowed. Since he didn\'t succeed, the boy climbed a nearby mango tree so as to watch the match. And so he was able to watch the match without a ticket.\nIt was indeed a tough match as neither of the two teams conceded a goal. They played full-time and there were no scores. They were given extra time. It ended goalless:\n\n The teams involved in the football match were? ','Party Club and School Club','Enyimba Football Club and Yankari Football Club','Debate Club and Mathematics Club','','','B',1,'',1),(2,'Where was the match held? ','Jokolo Amusement Park','Jokolo Stadium ','Abuja Stadium  ','Enyimba Stadium','','B',1,'',2),(3,'How did the small boy get to the gateman at the stadium?  ','He flipped one of his legs','He walked sluggishly to the gate','He pushed his way between the legs of the crowd','He danced his way through the crowd','','C',1,'',3),(4,'What did the boy take out of his pocket?',' A letter from his father ','','Nothing ','A stone','','D',1,'',4),(5,'How did the match end?','Happily   ','In chaos','Enyimba Football Club won with 2 goals','Goalless','','D',1,'',5),(6,'Citizens should always pay their ----------- to enable government provide social amenities for them. (','bills ','charges ','fees ','tax','','D',1,'',6),(7,' The woman did not get married, she died as a ______','bachelor ','bride ','partner ','spinster','','D',1,'',7),(8,'A ________ of people gathered at the accident scene','crowd   ','colony   ','horde','host','','A',1,'',8),(9,'Many ________ sat for our school?s Common Entrance Examination.','applicants','candidates ','people ','students','','B',1,'',9),(10,'______ is the output device that displays visual information from the computer','Hard Drive','Hardware    ','Monitor    ','Keyboard','','C',1,'',10),(11,'The ________ pronounced the accused guilty','clerk   ','registrar   ','lawyer','judge','','D',1,'',11),(12,'Mining is the means of ________ economically important minerals and ores deposits below the earths surface.','extraction   ','distributing   ','destroying   ','extracting','','D',1,'',12),(13,'We gave our teacher a ________ of flowers','banquet ','collection ','pack','bouquet','','D',1,'',13),(14,'The ________ in the prison complained that the condition of the prison was becoming unbearable','inmates ','criminals ','detainees ','robbers','','A',1,'',14),(15,'Bola visited a ________ when he had a toothache','pharmacist  ','dentist','pediatrician   ','physio