y close to the surface, it is -29- by huge','Raked','Removed','Harvested','dug out','','D',1,'',29),(30,'huge ? 30-. This is called open cast mining. Strip mining is the name of the method used when the material is covered by only a layer of other matter-usually soil or clayWhen the substance is -31-, i.e. found in river bed deposits, buckets or suction dredgers can be used to extract itBut many materials lie far below the surface. Some, like -32-and salt, may be brought to the surface by other meansBut in most cases, a deep shaft has to be sunk to give -33- access','Excavating machines','Hoe','Axe','Cutlass','','A',1,'',30),(31,'When the substance is -31-, i.e. found in river bed deposits, buckets or suction dredgers can be used to extract it','stiff ','Alluvial','Dark','Red','','B',1,'',31),(32,'But many materials lie far below the surface. Some, like -32-and salt, may be brought to the surface by other means.','Patrol','Gas','Sulphur','Kerosine','','C',1,'',32),(33,'But in most cases, a deep shaft has to be sunk to give -33- access','Harvesters','Planters','Diggers','Miners','','D',1,'',33),(34,'access to the -34-where the veins of ore are','rock surface','River','Engine','Plant','','A',1,'',34),(35,'Long passages, called galleries, must be -35-. The roofs and sides of the galleries need  to be shored up to prevent them from collapsing under the weight of earth above them','Excavated','Swept','Generated','Planted','','C',1,'',35),(36,'Complete each of the following sentences with the most appropriate of the options lettered A to D (nos 36-45): She loves to read, ________ he enjoys playing music.','and ','nor ','so ','yet','','A',1,'',36),(37,'They wanted to go to the beach, ________ it started raining','yet  ','but','unless   ','or','','B',1,'',37),(38,'He broke the glass cup, ________ he?','did  ','does  ','didn?t  ','doesn\'t','','C',1,'',38),(39,'They are not coming today, ________ they? ','aren\'t  ','isn\'t  ','won\'t  ','are','','D',1,'',39),(40,'John is the ________ boy in his class.','most smartest','more smartest','smart ','smartest','','D',1,'',40),(41,'He has met the ________ for admission into the school','creteria ','criteria','critteria ','criterria','','B',1,'',41),(42,'Would like some ________ after dinner? ','desserrt   ','desert  ','dessert','desserte','','C',1,'',42),(43,'They did the work ________','ourself  ','ourselves  ','theirselves  ','themselves','','D',1,'',43),(44,'Active Voice: The striker is scoring the winning goal. Passive Voice: The winning goal ________ scored by the striker.','is being','has been ','has being','had been','','A',1,'',44),(45,'The sentence, ?We travelled to Kano last week?, said the students, re-written in indirect speech form becomes, ?The student said that _____','they travelled to Kano last week','they travelled to Kano the following week','they travelled to Kano the previous week','they travelled to Kano this week','','C',1,'',45),(46,'/i?/','near ','dare ','browse ','bring','','A',1,'',46),(47,'/u?/','sure ','fair ','bright ','crunch','','A',1,'',47),(48,'/t/','slapped ','thick ','them ','anthem','','A',1,'',48),(49,'/d/','mother ','father ','brother ','maiden','','D',1,'',49),(50,'/?/','think  ','that  ','rather  ','mother','','A',1,'',50),(51,'/ai/','quay ','bye ','toy ','bit','','B',1,'',51),(52,'/b/','lamb ','comb ','bomb ','plumb','','D',1,'',52),(53,'/?/','top ','about ','flood ','ensure','','C',1,'',53),(54,'/?i/','bouy ','foot ','fail ','rice','','A',1,'',54),(55,'/a:/','cat ','beach ','mat ','mar','','D',1,'',55),(56,'?The sky is pregnant? is an example of what figure of speech?','metaphor','personification ','simile ','hyperbole','','B',1,'',56),(57,'A form of Literature that is meant to be performed on for an audience is _____','novel ','poem ','drama ','novelette','','C',1,'',57),(58,'After the death of King Adebanji ________ is crowned as the next king.','Adetusa','Aderonbi    ','Adelegan    ','Balogun','','C',1,'',58),(59,'_____ is Baba Fagbemi?s son.','Fa