INSERT INTO `geogcat2quest299` VALUES (1,'Which of the following truly represents a spot height?   A. D192   B. ?BM 520  C. ?347   D. ?BM','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',1),(2,'?? A long and narrow hill usually represented by series of elongated contour lines that runs almost parallel to each other is A. Contour line    B. Ridge   C. Spur    D. Valley.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',2),(3,'1.????? Round top and conical hills are similar in that their contours are A. Circular. B. Rectangular. C. Steep slope.                D. Angular.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',3),(4,'4A spur is a projection of which of the following into lowlands?  A. headland. B.  cataract. C. stack. D. valley','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',4),(5,'5Which type of drainage pattern is shown above?  A. Dendritic     B. Trellised    C. Radial pattern    D. Annular drainage pattern.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',5),(6,'6 These are simple points on the ground making the angles of triangulation when mapping an area. They are usually represented by a triangle and a dot in the middle with the height written by the side. This describes a A. Spot height   B. Trigonometrical Station   Coresidential area   D. knoll','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',6),(7,'Which of the following is not land transportation? (A) Road transportation (B) Rail transportation (C) Pipeline transportation (D) None of the above','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',7),(8,'8?It is flexible, because it can move persons or goods from door to door?.  This description is characteristic of which of the following (A) Air (B) Road (C) Water (D) Rail. type of transportation? ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',8),(9,'9.All but ONE of these is not an advantage of road transportation.(A)  It is flexible, because it can move persons or goods from door to door.(B) It is faster than some other transport. (C) Materials can be transported from most remote areas to urban area(D) It is slow type of transportation','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',9),(10,'The roles of transportation in the economic development of West Africa include the following except  A. NATIONAL disintegration       B. Movement of goods and services  C. Opening up of new lands  D. Provision of employment','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',10),(11,'Which of these can be considered as the earliest means of water transportation?A. Speed boat  B. Cargo ship  C. Train  D. Paddle canoe ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',11),(12,' One major advantage of water transport over other types of transport is thatA. It is the cheapest for the transportation of bulky goods.   B. It is flexible.   C. It is void of disaster.   D. It cannot be disturbed by storm','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',12),(13,'1.?????? All but one of these is an advantage of road transportation. A. It is flexible, because it can move persons or goods from door to door.   B. It is faster than some other transport means.   C. It is very cheap.   D. It is the only means of transport that can move bulky goods.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',13),(14,'14???? Which of the following is not land transportation? A. Road transportation.   B. Rail transportation.   C. Pipeline transportation.   D. None of the above','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',14),(15,'15??? Which of the following is a heavy industry? (a) Petroleum industry (b) paper mill industry (c) textile industry (d) confectionary industry.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',15),(16,'16.??? Which of the following industry is best located near the source of raw material?(a) drug manufacturing (b) paint manufacturing (c) sugar manufacturing (d) watch making','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',16),(17,'17??? One of the major problems of manufacturing industries is (a) high quality of the industrial labour (b) high cost of labour (c) (c) inadequate raw material (d) over production of manufactured goods.  (c)inadequate raw material (d) over production of manufactured goods. ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',17),(18,'18 All the following activities belong to primary industries except (a). Lumbering (b). Quarrying (c) processing (d). fishing','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',18),(19,'? The class of manufacturing industries that produced goods like meat, dairy products, beer, coffee, biscuits etc. are referred to as (a). Light industries (b). Banking (c). Heavy industries (d). Consumer goods industries.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',19),(20,'14??? Textile industries are best located in northern Nigeria because of A. Availability of cotton. B. High demand for cotton materials. C. Availability of capital. D.  Availability of heavy machinery','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',20);
