INSERT INTO `geogquest725` VALUES (1,'1.-------- are the various signs used by map makers to represent both natural and cultural features on the map. A.Map Keys B. Conventional Symbols C. line Signs D. Sign Language.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',1),(2,'2.All these are types of map EXCEPT A. Atlas map B. Sketch map C. Photographic map D.Topographical Map.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',2),(3,'Map producers are also called---- A. Artist B. Teachers C. Cartographers D. Geologists','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',3),(4,'4.The type of map that is commonly used in schools, colleges by examination bodies is ----- A. Atlas MapB. Sketch Map C. Topographic Map D. Plan Maps.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',4),(5,'5. .A map that provides required information to be used by airplane pilots and ship captians is called. A.Weather map B. Sketch map C. Topographical map D. Plan map','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',5),(6,'6. If the scale of a map is 2cm to 1km, what is the ground distance if the distance between the two places on the\nmap is 10cm? A. 20km B. 10km C. 5km D. 15km','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',6),(7,'7. If the scale of a map is 1:200,000, what is the map distance between two towns if the distance on the ground is20km? A. 20cm B.10cm C.15cm D.18cm','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',7),(8,'8. When the scale of the new map to be drawn is larger than the original map extract it means, it means A. Map Enlargement B.Map Reduction C.Grid lines D. Convectional lines.  ','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',8),(9,' When the scale of the new map to be drawn is larger than the original map extract it means, it means A. Map Enlargement B.Map Reduction C.Grid lines D. Convectional lines.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',9),(10,'10. Convert 1:300,000 to statement scale A. 1cm to 5km B. 1cm to 3km C. 2cm to 10km D. 1cm to 10km.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',10),(11,'The above map is an example of   a.Plan map b. Atlas map c.Topographical map d. Route map','A','B','C','D','','C',0.5,'',11),(12,'12. 1 cm to 1 km is the same as a.1: 10000  b. 1: 100,000  c. 1: 200,000  d, 1: 50,000','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',12),(13,'13. All but one of the following is not a type of scale used in map reading   a.?? Measuring scale  b. Statement scale  c. Linear scale  d  Representative Fraction','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',13),(14,'a.?????? 14. Which of the following is a large scale? A. 1:1000,000  b. 1:250  c. 1:500,000 d. 1:2000,000','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',14),(15,'15. A map representing land-use features is called a, Cadastral map b.  Route map  c.. Atlas map  d       Plan map','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',15),(16,'Use the Attached map of MOLAI S.W to answer question 16-20','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',16),(17,'16. What is the scale of the map in representative fraction?(a)1: 50,000 (b) 1: 200,000 (c) 1: 100,000 (d) 1: 25, 000','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',17),(18,'17. The highest contour line on the map is (a) 140m (b) 120m (c) 20m (d) 145m','A','B','C','D','','A',0.5,'',18),(19,'18. What is the contour interval on the map? (a) 50 (b) 100 (c) 25 (d) 20','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',19),(20,'19.?What is the likely occupation of LERE settlement? (a) Lumbering (b) farming (c) mining (d) fishing','A','B','C','D','','D',0.5,'',20),(21,'19.?One noticeable manmade feature along the road linking DAKKA and UVU settlement can best be described as (a) plantation farm (b) a bridge (c) a dam (d) a market.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.5,'',21);
