INSERT INTO `geogss2cat2quest213` VALUES (1,'. The major source of power for most terrestrial ecosystems is A. geothermal energy.B. hydroelectric power. C. solar energy. D. nuclear power.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',1),(2,'Figure 2 below shows a feeding relationship in an ecosystem. Use it to answer questions 2 and 3The feeding relationship above shows a :Figure 2 ; Grass---Grasshopper----lizard---snake---Hawk A. symbiotic relationship. B. parasitic relationship.\nC. food chain. D. food web.\n','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',2),(3,'3. Which of the following is a primary producer? A. Snake. B. Lizard. C. Grass. D. Grasshopper.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',3),(4,'4. The relationship between the elements of an ecosystem is best described as A. parasitic. Symbiotic. C. multidirectional. Interdependent.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',4),(5,'The study of the continuous interaction between living things and their environments is known as A.Ecology. B. Energy cycle. C. Biology. D. Geology.','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',5),(6,'. The dynamic and interdependent complex interaction of soil, climate and vegetation with its animal population is called A. food chain.B. ecosystem. C. carbon cycle. D. hydrological cycle.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',6),(7,'Autotrophs, heterotrophs and decomposers are associated with A. Vegetation. B. Climate C. Ecosystem. D. Geology. ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',7),(8,'8. Environmental balance includes all the following except A. hydrological cycle. B. carbon cycle. C. food chain and food web. D. earthquake cycle','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',8),(9,'. 9. Nature mostly intervenes in the state of balance in land ecosystem through A. Earth\'s revolution. B. Climatic change. C. Earth equilibrium. D. Earth rotation.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',9),(10,'10. Which of the following is not associated with human intervention? A. Mining. B. Construct on C  Rainfall. D Urbanization. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',10),(11,'11. Which of the following environmental hazards is prevalent in the coastal area? A Drought B Deforestation. C. Pollution. D. Flooding','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',11),(12,'12. A community of plants and animals living in harmony within the same physical environment is referred to as A. environmental interaction. B. terrestrial bicycle. C. ecosystem. D. biosphere.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',12),(13,'13. The release of harmful substances into the environment is called A. flooding. B. drought. C. harmattan. D. pollution. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',13),(14,'14. A disaster caused by nature or man which poses a serious danger to lives and properties of the people is called environmental  A. intervention. B. hazard. C. interaction. D. change. ','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',14),(15,'15. Which of the following are water pollutants? A. Aquatic animals. B. Shrimps. C Dissolved fertilizers. D. Water plants. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',15),(16,'. All the following are environmental hazards except A. flooding. B vulcanicity C. afforestation. D deforestation.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',16),(17,'A negative effect of mineral exploitation is A. afforestation. B. hydration. C. pollution. D oxidation. ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',17),(18,'18. Which of the following environmental hazards is due primarily to human activities? A. Earthquake .B Volcanic eruption. C. Hurricane. D. Ozone depletion.','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',18),(19,'Possible solutions to the problem of soil erosion in the highlands of West Africa include all the following except A. indiscriminate felling of trees. B. rotational grazing. C. strip cultivation. D. planting of shelter belts.','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',19),(20,'. Water pollution is caused by all the following except A. treated sewage. B. industrial waste. C. oil spillage. D. fishing with chemicals. ','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',20);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `geogss2cat2quest213` ENABLE KEYS */;
