INSERT INTO `physs2cat23rdtermquest498` VALUES (1,' When a plane mirror on which a ray is incident is rotated through an angle of 10? , to what angle will the reflected ray be rotated? A. 20 degree B. 10degree C. 30degreesD. 40degree','20 degree','10 degree','30 degree','40 degree','','A',1,'',1),(2,' A An equilateral glass prism of refractive index 1.5 , produces a minimum deviation when a ray of light strikes on one face. Calculate the angle of minimum deviation. A. 51.48o      B. 65.50o     C. 91.53o       D. 37.2o ','51.48 degree','65.50 degree','91.53 degree','37.2 degree','','D',1,'',2),(3,' the angle of incidence in the denser medium for which the angle of refraction is 900 when light travels from a denser medium to a less dense medium is referred to as  A. critical mass      B. total internal relected angle        C. angle of deviation        D. critical angle','critical mass','total internal reflected angle','angle of deviation','critical angle','','D',1,'',3),(4,' The refractive index of a material is 1.5. Calculate the critical angle at the glass-air interface.  A. 19?     B. 21?      C. 39?      D. 42?','19 degrees','21 degrees','39 degres','42 degrees','','D',1,'',4),(5,' Total internal reflection occurs in an optical prism when light rays A. travel from the prism into an optically denser medium     B. are incident in the prism at an angle greater than the critical angle      C. are incident normally in the prism      D. travel from the prism to air','travelss from the prism into an optically dense medium','are incident in the prism at an angle greater than the critical angle','are incident normally in the prism','travel from the prism to air','','B',1,'',5),(6,' A swimming pool is 2.1m deep. If it contains water of refractive index 1.3, calculate the apparent depth of the pool.    A. 3.4m        B. 2.7m       C. 1.6m        D. 0.8m','3.4 m','2.7 m','1.6 m','0.8 m','','C',1,'',6),(7,' A ray of light passes from air to water to glass to air. Given that the refractive index for light passing from air to water is  4/3 and air to glass is  3/2 , calculate the refractive index of glass relative to water.       A. 0.50      B. 0.67      C. 0.75      D. 1.13','0.5','0.67','0.75','1.13','','D',1,'',7),(8,'&lt;p&gt;The diagram below shows the prism arrangement in a A. binocular B. spectrometer C. periscope D. Projector&lt;/p&gt;\n\n&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1962786687.png&quot; style=&quot;height:128px; width:197px&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;binocular&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;spectrometer&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;periscope&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;projector&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',1,'',8),(9,' The speed of light in a certain medium is V while its speed in a vacuum is C. The absolute refractive index of the medium is  A. C + V      B. C/V      C. V/C      D. C ? V','C + V','C/V','V/C','C - V','','B',1,'',9),(10,'To obtain a virtual, erect and magnified image from a thin converging lens, an object must be placed                 A. between the focus and the lens. B. at the focus.  C. between the focus and twice the focal length.                  D. beyond twice the focal length.','between the focus and the lens','at the focus','between the focus and twice the focal length','beyond twice the dfocal length','','A',1,'',10),(11,' Images formed by a diverging lens are always  A. erect, real and magnified    B. inverted, real and diminished     C. erect, virtual and diminished  D. inverted, virtual and magnified.','erect, real and magnified','inverted, real and diminished','erect, virtual and diminished','inverted, virtual and magnified','','C',1,'',11),(12,'An object is placed at a point X between the focal point F and the optical center C of a diverging lens. If F? is the focal point on the other side of the lens, the image of the object is formed between A. F and X                   B. X and C         C. C and F?       D.   F? and  2F?','A and X','X and C','C and F\'','F\' and 2F\'','','A',1,'',12),(13,' The angle of incidence in the denser medium for which the angle of refraction is 900 when light travels from a denser medium to a less dense medium. A. critica angle      B refractive index       C. absolute refactive index       D. critical mass','critical angle','refractive index','absolute refractive index','critical mass','','A',1,'',13),(14,' A diverging lens of focal length 30cm produces an image 20cm from the lens. Determine the object distance.   A. 10cm      B. 12cm      C. 50cm      D. 60cm','10 cm','12 cm','50 cm','60 cm','','D',1,'',14),(15,' The unit of power of lens is     A. decimeter        B. watt      C. dioptre      D. decibel','decimeter','watt','dioptre','decibel','','C',1,'',15),(16,'Which of the following optical devices employs the use of diverging lens?     A. Astronomical telescope     B. Compound microscope   C. Kaleidoscope      D. Galilean telescope','Astronomical telescope','compound microscope','kaleidoscope','Galilean telescope','','D',1,'',16),(17,'A telescope is said to be in normal adjustment when the          A. Focal length of objective is greater than that of the eyepiece        B. Focal length of the eyepiece is greater than that of the objective        C. Focal length of the eyepiece is equal to that of the objective       D. Objective focal point coincides with that of the eyepiece','focal length of objective is greater than that of the eyepiece','focal length of the eyepiece is greater than that of the objective','focal length of the eyepiece is equal to that of the objective','objective focal point coincides with that of the eyepiece','','D',1,'',17),(18,' The focal length of the eyepiece of an astronomical telescope is f_e, while the focal length of the objective  is f_o. For normal adjustment, the angular magnification is given  by A. f_o/f_e      B. 1-  f_o/f_e     C. f_o/f_e -1    D. f_e/f_o ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',18),(19,'Complementary colours are those which A. have the same reflective index. B. have the same wavelength. C. add-up to produce black light.  D. add-up to produce white light.','have te same reflective index','have the same wavelength','add-up to produce black light','add-up to produce white light','','D',1,'',19),(20,'20. Which of the sets of colored light is/are secondary colors?\nI. Red, Blue and Green\nII. Blue, Cyan and Magenta\nIII. Green, Magenta and Yellow\nIV. Yellow, Cyan and Magenta \nA. I and II only     B.   II and III only       C.   IV only         D. I, II and IV only\n','I and II only','II and III only','IV only','I, II and IV only','','C',1,'',20);
