INSERT INTO `ss1crscat23rdterm2025quest752` VALUES (1,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;What does &amp;ldquo;impartiality&amp;rdquo; mean? A. Treating all people equally without bias. B. Favoring friends and family. C. Judging others quickly. D. Discriminating based on status.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(2,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;In Christian belief, why are all human beings considered equal before God? A. Because all are created in God&amp;rsquo;s image. B. Because God shows favoritism to some. C. Because only certain nations are chosen.D. Because wealth determines God&amp;rsquo;s favor.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(3,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Galatians 3:28 teaches that in Christ there is neither Jew nor Greek. What principle does this illustrate? A. All people are equal before God. B. Only Jews can enter the kingdom. C. The Old Testament laws must be kept by Christians. D. Gentiles are inferior to Jews.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(4,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which Bible verse explicitly states that God shows no partiality among people? A. Acts 10:34 B. Mark 12:30 C. Luke 1:37 D. John 3:16&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(5,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;According to James 2:1-13, showing favoritism toward the rich and ignoring the poor in the church is: A. A demonstration of wisdom. B. Sinful, because God is impartial. C. Required for salvation. D. An unimportant issue.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(6,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;The &amp;ldquo;Golden Rule&amp;rdquo; as taught by Jesus in Matthew 7:12 and Luke 6:31 instructs us to: A. Treat others as you yourself want to be treated. B. Judge others before you are judged. C. Love only those who love you. D. Seek personal advantage first.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(7,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;What does &amp;ldquo;nepotism&amp;rdquo; refer to? A. Favoring relatives or friends in hiring or promotion. B. A strict merit-based system. C. Treating everyone with complete equality. D. Randomly selecting people for jobs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(8,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Nepotism and favoritism in society often result in: A. Fair and transparent decisions. B. Unfairness and reduced trust. C. Higher efficiency and talent. D. Equal opportunities for all.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(9,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Tribalism in a nation tends to lead to: A. Greater unity among different groups. B. Conflict and division between groups. C. Elimination of social tensions. D. Equal treatment for everyone.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(10,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which of the following best demonstrates impartial behavior? A. Welcoming both a rich person and a poor person to church equally. B. Providing seats only for the well-dressed. C. Favoring one&amp;rsquo;s own tribe or family in decisions. D. Hiring only friends despite qualifications.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(11,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which individuals were the first to visit Jesus&amp;rsquo; tomb on the morning of the resurrection? A. Jesus&amp;rsquo; female followers (the women). B. The Roman soldiers guarding the tomb. C. The disciples Peter and John. D. The chief priests and Pharisees.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(12,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;In the synoptic Gospels, what instruction did the angel(s) at the tomb give the women? A. Remain silent and leave the tomb. B. Return home and wait for news. C. Go and tell the disciples that Jesus has risen.D. Anoint the body again with spices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0),(13,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which event is mentioned only in Matthew&amp;rsquo;s account of the resurrection? A. An earthquake that rolled back the stone. B. Women named Joanna and Mary visiting the tomb. C. The women fleeing in fear.D. Two angels standing at the tomb.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(14,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Why were the women visiting Jesus&amp;rsquo; tomb according to Luke 24:1-11? A. To anoint Jesus&amp;rsquo; body with spices. B. To meet with the disciples. C. To ask the chief priests a question. D. To check if Jesus has resurrected from the death.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(15,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Why is the resurrection of Jesus central to the Christian faith? A. It demonstrates God&amp;rsquo;s power over death and assures believers of eternal life. B. It allows Christians to ignore the Ten Commandments. C. It indicates that Jesus&amp;rsquo; teachings were myths. D. It proves that Jesus was not a human.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(16,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;What role did Mary Magdalene and the other women have in the resurrection story? A. They discovered the empty tomb and informed the disciples. B. They witnessed Jesus&amp;rsquo; defeat of satan on Easter morning. C. They challenged the guards who were posted at the tomb. D. They wrote the Gospel accounts of the resurrection.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(17,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which woman is &lt;em&gt;not&lt;/em&gt; mentioned as visiting Jesus&amp;rsquo; tomb in the synoptic accounts? A. Mary Magdalene B. Salome C. Joanna D. Martha&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',0),(18,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which Gospel uniquely records that the Jewish leaders bribed the tomb guards to lie about the resurrection? A. Matthew B. Mark C. Luke D. John&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',0),(19,'&lt;ol start=&quot;11&quot;&gt;\n	&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri,&amp;quot;sans-serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Jesus told his followers to meet him in ________ after his resurrection, according to the synoptic Gospels.&lt;br /&gt;\n	A. Jerusalem B. Galilee C. Nazareth D. Bethlehem&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;\n&lt;/ol&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',0),(20,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:12.0pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Baskerville Old Face&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;serif&amp;quot;&quot;&gt;Which Gospel mentions two men (angels) at the empty tomb who told the women that Jesus had risen?&lt;br /&gt;\nA. Matthew B. Mark C. Luke D. John&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;br /&gt;\n&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0);
