INSERT INTO `ss1econcat13rdtermquest697` VALUES (1,'1. Which of the following is a function of merchant banks A. acting as banker\'s bank. B. Lending to the commercial banks as a last resort. C. Controlling inflation in the economy. D. Underwriting and issuing of shares. ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',1),(2,'2. Which of the following is an asset of a commercial bank A. Reserve funds. B. Shareholder\'s capital. C. Customer\'s deposits. D. Treasury bills. ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',2),(3,'3. The drawer of a cheque is the A. person who is to be paid the sum of money as written on the cheque. B. person who takes the cheque to the bank. C. bank e on which the cheque is drawn. D. person who writes out the cheque. ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',3),(4,'4. The financial institution that specializes in risk spreading is called A. an investment bank. B. a development bank. C. an insurance company. D. the stock exchange. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',4),(5,'5. The clearing house of all commercial banks in Nigeria is the A. General Post Office. B. Bank for Commerce and Industry. C. Nigerian Industrial Development Bank. D. Central Bank','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',5),(6,'6. Deposits held in a commercial bank are part of A. money supply. B. transfer payments. C. ordinary shares. D. treasury bills.','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',6),(7,'7. Time deposit has the same meaning as A. current account. B. demand deposit. C. fixed deposit account. D. bank deposit. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',7),(8,'8. All rates of interest in a country are influenced by the A. bank rate. B. population growth rate. C. Wage rate. D. mortgage rate.','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',8),(9,'9. The amount of money to be created by commercial banks is actually influenced by the A. legal reserve ratio. B. external reserve. C. external borrowing. D. availability of money and capital market. ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',9),(10,'10. A financial institution established for the purpose of providing specialized services like acceptance of bills of exchange and equipment leasing is known as A. merchant Bank. B. development Bank. C. central Bank. D. insurance Company.','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',10),(11,'11. Which of the following is a liability of a commercial bank A. Deposits. B. Money at call. C. Loans to customers. D. Overdrafts. ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',11),(12,'12. Commercial banks settle their inter-bank indebtedness through A. merchant banks. B. central bank. C. development banks. D. stock exchange. ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',12),(13,'13. Which of the following banks grant credit facilities to individuals wishing to build houses A. Central Bank of Nigeria. B. Nigerian Industrial Development Bank. C. Agricultural Credit Bank. D. Federal Mortgage Bank of Nigeria. ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',13),(14,'14. The primary objective of the Nigerian Industrial Development Bank (NIDB) is the provision of loans to A. farmers. B. manufacturers. C. estate agents. D. transporters. ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',14),(15,'15. The proportion of commercial bank\'s total assets kept in the form of highly liquid assets is known as A. demand deposit. B. fixed deposit. C. cash ratio. D. moral suasion. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',15),(16,'16. A cheque book is issued to customers of a bank operating a A. savings account. B. time deposit account. C. current account. D. fixed deposit account. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',16),(17,'17. Which of the following is a bank\'s responsibility to its shareholders A. Making profits. B. Creating money. ibn C. Paying high interest rate. D. preventing inflation.','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',17),(18,'18. Development banks mainly provide A. savings account facilities for a developing economy B. foreign exchange facilities for importers and exporters. C. capital for development of specific sectors. D. capital for hire purchase. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',18),(19,'19. Tools of monetary policy do not include A. open market operations. B. reserve requirement. C. bank rate. D. tax and public expenditure.  ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',19),(20,'20. Mortgage banks give loans to investors on long term basis to A. finance agriculture. B. establish banks. C. acquire machinery. D. build houses.','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',20);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `ss1econcat13rdtermquest697` ENABLE KEYS */;
