INSERT INTO `ss2chemcat2quest800` VALUES (1,'1. An example of an element that can catenate is, A. carbon  B. nitrogen C. bromine D. chlorine','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',1),(2,'principal constituent of natural gas is, A. methane B. propane C. butane D. ethane','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',2),(3,'1. The chief source of hydrocarbons is, A. natural gas B. coal  C. methane D. petroleum','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',3),(4,'4. Which of the following compounds is aromatic? A. Toluene B. Cyclobutane C. Hexane D. Cyclopropane','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',4),(5,'5. The following compounds are hydrocarbons except, A. 2- methylbutane B. methylpropanoate C. benzene D. cyclohexane','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',5),(6,'6. Which of the following hydrocarbons is unsaturated? A. Ethane B. Benzene C. Propane D. 2,2,4-trimethylpentane','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',6),(7,'7. Alkanes react with halogens mainly by, A. oxidation B. addition C. substitution D. polymerization','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',7),(8,'8. How many carbon atoms are present in one molecule of 2- methylpropane? A. 2 B. 3  C. 4  D. 5','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',8),(9,'9. The IUPAC name of the compound CF3CHBrCl is, A. 2-chloro-2-bromo-1,1,1- trifluoroethane B. 1- bromo-1- chloro- 2,2,2-trifluoroethane C. 1,1,1-trifluoro-2- bromo-2-chloroethane D. 2- bromo- 2-chloro-1,1.1-trifluoroethane','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',9),(10,'10. CH3COONa(s) + NaOH(s) ?Na2CO3(s) + X(g). In the reaction X represents, A. ethane B. methane C. water D. hydrogen','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',10),(11,'11. How many isomers can be obtained from C4H10? A. 1  B. 0  C. 3  D. 2','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',11),(12,'12. What is the main type of reaction alkenes undergo? A. Addition B. Condensation C. Elimination D. Substitution','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',12),(13,'13. The reagent can be used to distinguish ethene from ethyne is, A. benedict solution B. ammoniacal silver trioxonitrate (V) solution C. bromine water D. fehling?s solution','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',13),(14,'14. Hydrocarbons which react with ammoniacal copper (l) chloride solution conform to the general molecular formula A. CnH2n B. CnH2n C. CnH2n+2 D. CnH2n-2','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',14),(15,'15. Alkenes undergo the following reactions except, A. addition B. hydration C. polymerization D. substitution','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',15),(16,'16. Why is carbon often deposited in the exhaust-pipe of cars? A. Presence of carbon in petrol B. Incomplete combustion of petrol C. presence of additives in petrol D. complete combustion of petrol','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',16),(17,'17. What is the molar mass of an alkyne with the formula CxH14? (H = 1, C = 12) A. 86g B. 92g C. 98g D. 110g','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',17),(18,'18. The colour of the solution formed when ethyne reacts with an acidified solution of potassium tetraoxomanganate (VII) is, A. pink B. colourless C. purple D. green','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',18),(19,'19. When water drops on calcium carbide, the gaseous product is an, A. alkanol B. alkyne C. alkene D. alkane','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',19),(20,'20. The gas given off when ethanol reacts with sodium metal is, A. Carbon (IV) oxide B. methane C. hydrogen D. oxygen','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',20);
