INSERT INTO `ss2econcat13rdtermquest640` VALUES (1,'1. It is important to measure the National Income of a country because A. It is a major determinant of the standard of living B. It reveals hazards of development like pollution and congestion C. It reveals the distribution of the citizens? savings in foreign banks D. Its size determines the extent of political stability ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',1),(2,'2. Near money is made up of (a) very liquid assets which cannot be converted into money (b) currency in circulation and demand deposits (c) notes and coins (d) fixed assets which cannot be converted into money. ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',2),(3,'3. GDP is a :A. Good measure of relative welfare in various countries B. Good measure of relative prices in various countries C. Good measure of relative living standards in various countries D. Good measure of market activities at market prices ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',3),(4,'4. In national income accounting, double counting occurs when A. Intermediate goods are counted twice B. Intermediate goods are counted with the final goods. C. Final goods are counted more than once. D. Different people count the product. ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',4),(5,'5. The difference between GDP and GNP is. A. Consumption of fixed capital B. Indirect business tax. C. Net factor income from abroad. D. Public transfer payments. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',5),(6,'6. Which of the following items is not included in the measurement of the national income using the income approach? A. Wages and salaries B. Government purchases C. Interest D. Dividend','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',6),(7,'7. If the money supply doubles while real output and velocity remain constant, according to the Quantity Theory of Money, what will happen to the price level? a) It will double b) It will remain the same c) It will halve d) It will decrease by a quarter ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',7),(8,'8. The Quantity Theory of Money focuses on the relationship between changes in the money supply and changes in: a) Unemployment rate b) Real GDP c) Consumer preferences d) Exchange rates ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',8),(9,'9. According to the Quantity Theory of Money, if the central bank increases the money supply at a rate of 5% and real GDP grows at a rate of 3%, what is the expected rate of inflation? a) 2% b) 3% c) 5% d) 8%','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',9),(10,'In the Quantity Theory of Money, if the velocity of money (V) increases while the money supply and real GDP remain constant, what is the effect on the price level? a) It increases b) It decreases c) It remains the same d) It depends on the rate of inflation ','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',10),(11,'11. The Quantity Theory of Money is often used to explain the relationship between changes in the money supply and changes in the: a) Trade balance b) Exchange rate c) Velocity of money d) Price level','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',11),(12,'12. Inflation is best defined as: a) A decrease in the general price level b) A sustained increase in the general price level c) A decrease in the money supply d) A decrease in the aggregate demand ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',12),(13,'13. Inflation results in: a) Increased purchasing power b) Decreased purchasing power c) No change in purchasing power d) Increased real wages ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',13),(14,'14. Demand-pull inflation occurs when: a) The cost of production decreases b) Aggregate demand exceeds aggregate supply c) The money supply decreases d) Interest rates rise significantly ','A','B','C','D','','B',1,'',14),(15,'15. Cost-push inflation is primarily caused by: a) Excessive aggregate demand b) An increase in the money supply c) A decrease in production costs d) A decrease in wages ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',15),(16,'16. What is stagflation? a) A period of high inflation and low economic growth b) A period of high inflation and high economic growth c) A period of low inflation and low economic growth d) A period of low inflation and high economic growth','A','B','C','D','','A',1,'',16),(17,'17. Given the present state of the Nigerian economy, which of the following measures will promote a more rapid economic development? (a) Complete dependence on oil exports (b) Concentration on agricultural exports (c) Diversification of the economy (d) Building of more schools and universities. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',17),(18,'18. Which of the following is used for measuring national Income? A. Output income and wages. B. Import expenditure and output. C. Income, output and expenditure. D. Export, import and output. ','A','B','C','D','','C',1,'',18),(19,'19. Exclusions that make Gross National Product a poor measure of welfare are A. government purchases B. govern ment military outlays C. wages and sala ries D. housewives\' services. ','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',19),(20,'20. In national income accounting. NNP is derived by subtracting -------- from the GNP A. transfer payments B. indirect taxes C. allowance for wastage D. capital consumption.','A','B','C','D','','D',1,'',20);
