INSERT INTO `ss2fmathscat2thirdtermquest468` VALUES (1,'1.in a single throw of two fair coins, find the probability that two heads appear.\nA)    1/2         B)  1/4           C)   3/4           D)2/3  ','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(2,'2.A and B are two independent events such that P(A) =2/5  and P(AnB)=1/15.Find P(B)      \n','&lt;p&gt;3/5&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;1/6&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;5/8&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;2/15&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(3,'3.Events M and N are mutually exclusive. If P(M)=3/5  and P(MuN)=2/5,Find p(N)\n','&lt;p&gt;1/15&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;1/6&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;5/8&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;2/15&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(4,'The probability that Bola and Amaka will pass an examination are given as 0.8 and 0.9 respectively. Find the probability that at least one of them wil pass this examination. \n(A) 0.08	       (B) 0.98     (C) 0.72	(D)0.50','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(5,'Find the probability of obtaining 2 heads and a tail in 3 tosses of a fair coin.\n(A)1/13  	    ( B)1/8	     (C)3/8	          (D)5/16','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(6,'The probability that Jide, Atu and Obu solve a given problem are 1/12,1/7  and 1/4 respectively. Calculate the probability that all of them solves the problem.\n(A)	 1/336  (B)3/336  	  (C)1/112		(D)10/21','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(7,'A bag contains 5 red and 5 blue identical balls. Three balls are selected at random without replacement. Determine the probability of selecting balls alternating in colour.\n(A)7/18  	(B)5/9   	(C)5/36 	(D)1/36','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(8,' A and B are two independent events such that P(A) =7/12 and P(AnB)=1/2 .Find P(B)      (A)1/2	(B)	4/7	(C)	5/7	(D)6/7\n  ','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(9,'. In a class of 42 students consisting of 19 boys, two students are to be chosen at  random. Find the probability that the two students selected are of opposite sex but with a boy chosen first.\n(A)0.2538        (B)0.5075         (C)0.4534           (D)0.2477','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(10,'There are 25 yellow and x red identical balls in a bag. If the probability of selecting a red ball is , how many balls are in the bag?\n(A) 32   	(B)35    	(C)48	  (D)52','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(11,' Calculate the probability that the product of two numbers selected at random with replacement from the set {-3,-2,2,3} is positive.\n(A)1/3  (B)8/35  (C)4/35	 (D)1/2','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0),(12,' The annual demand for an electronic component is 8000 while the annual holding is ₦ 5.00. If the cost to place an order is ₦ 50.00, calculate the Economic Order Quantity (EOQ).\n(A) 160 000 units	(B) 8 000 units		(C) 400 units		(D) 4 000 units','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(13,' Inventory can be classified into the following except\n(A) Raw materials	(B)Waste materials(C) Finished goods 	(D) Goods for resale\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(14,' ............... describes the goods, materials, men, machine and money held available is stock by a business.\n	(A)Replacement		(B) Stock		(C) Inventory		(D) Materials','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(15,' The average cost is....................the ordering quantity(D).\n(A) Twice   (B) Half  (C) One-third   (D) Quarter','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(16,'Under replacement of items that fail completely and suddenly, two types of replacement policies may be considered namely;\n\n(A) Cooperate and Single			(B) Individual and group			(C) Individual and cooperate		(D) Single and group','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.5,'',0),(17,'The probability that a husband and a wife will be alive in 15 years’ time are  and  respectively. Find the probability that only one of them will be alive at that time\n(A)MN	    (B)M+N	(C)M+N-2MN	(D)1-MN','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.5,'',0),(19,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;Amount of order per annum to the nearest whole A. 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;8&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;B. 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;5&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;C. 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;2&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;D. 1&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;0&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.5,'',0),(20,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;The t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;ime between successive orders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;A.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;10days&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;B. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;5days&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;C. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;30days &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;D. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;20days&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.5,'',0)