INSERT INTO `ss2phy3rdtermcat1quest321` VALUES (1,'1.??????????? Which of the following is transmitted during wave motion? A. Power   B. Force  C. Energy  D. Moment    ','power','force','energy','moment','','C',1,'',1),(2,'2. A stone is dropped into the middle of a pool of water. Which of the following statements is/are correct?  (I) Spherical waves are set up in the water.    (II) The water moves outwards to the sides of the pool.    (III) Energy is transmitted outwards from the center of disturbance.   \nA.   I only        B.   II only          C.   III only       D.   I and III only\n','I only','II only','III only','I and III only','','D',1,'',2),(3,'3. A wave that requires a material medium for its? propagation is termed ----wave?      \n A. longitudinal                    B. transverse       C. electromagnetic      D. mechanical\n','Longitudinal','transverse','electromagnetic','mechanical','','D',1,'',3),(4,'4. The distance between two successive crests or trough in a wave front is called A. amplitude      B. wavelength       C. crest        D. period','amplitude','wavelength','crest','period','','B',1,'',4),(5,' A wave is represented by the equation    y = Asin 2?/? x. Which of the following statements about the wave is NOT correct? A. A represents the maximum displacement      B. The unit of y is the same as the unit of x    C. x is the distance of the particle from the origin      D. 2?x/? represents the wave number','A represents the maximum displacement','The unit of y is the samr as the unit of x','x is the distance of the particle from the origin','(2?x)/?','','A',1,'',5),(6,'6. A boat is rocked by waves of speed 30ms-1 whose successive crests are 10m apart. Calculate the rate at which the boat receives the waves A. 3.0ms-1     B. 30.3ms-1     C. 4.30ms-1    D. 3.50ms-1            ','3.0 m/s','30.3 m/s','4.3 ms','3.5 m/s','','D',1,'',6),(7,'7. Plane waves passing through a narrow gap emerge as circular waves. This phenomenon is known as       A. Interference      B. dispersion       C. refraction      D. diffraction','interference','dispersion','refraction','Diffraction','','D',1,'',7),(8,'8. Which of the following pairs of waves are both mechanical?  \nA. Light and sound        B. Microwave and water        C. Radio and light       D. Sound and water\n','light and sound','microwave and water','radio and light','sound and water','','D',1,'',8),(9,'9. When two waves are superimposed on each other, the following occurrences are possible, except                     A. Nodal lines     B. Anti-nodal lines      C. Stationary waves       D. Dispersion','Nodal lines','Anti-nodal lines','Stationary waves','Dispersion','','D',1,'',9),(10,'10. The superposition of waves to produce maximum or zero effect at a point is known as  \nA. reflection                   B. refraction      C. interference      D. diffraction.   \n','reflection','refraction','interference','diffraction','','B',1,'',10),(11,' Given that v, f and ? are the velocity, frequency and wavelength of a wave respectively. Which of the following equations is correct?   A.  f=v?    B. f=v/?   C. f=v/?^2     D. f=?/v^2 ','f = v?','f = v/?','f = v/?2','f = ?/v2','','D',1,'',11),(12,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;img alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/889971843.png&quot; style=&quot;height:176px; width:542px&quot; /&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',1,'',12),(13,' Calculate the frequency of the wave.     A.  100Hz     B.  200HzC.  30000Hz    D.  10000Hz','100 Hz','200 Hz','30000Hz','10000Hz','','D',1,'',13),(14,' A transverse wave can be distinguished from a longitudinal wave by \nA. Diffraction      B. Reflection     C. Refraction   D. Polarization\n','Diffraction','Reflection','Refraction','Polarization','','B',1,'',14),(15,' The distance between two points P and Q, along a wave is  0.05m. If the wavelength of the wave is 0.01m, determine the phase angle between P and Q in radians.   A. 0.1?    B. ?     C. 2?     D. 10?','0.1?','?','2?','10?','','A',1,'',15),(16,'Which of the point on the waveform are in phase? A. R and T       B. P and Q           C. R and S\n D. P and T.\n','R and T','P and Q','R and S','P and T','','B',1,'',16),(17,'A man 10 m in front of a large plane mirror. How far must he walk before he would be 5m away from is image?','5.0 m','7.5 m','10.0 m','12.5 m','','C',1,'',17),(18,'18. An object is placed in front of two plane mirrors inclined at 600 to each other. Determine the number of images formed.      A. 2      B. 3      C. 5       D. 7','2','3','5','7','','C',1,'',18),(19,'19. Which of the following phenomena is NOT a direct consequence of rectilinear propagation of light?        A. Lunar and solar eclipses B. Images of objects in a pinhole camera        C. Diffraction of light                  D. Shadows of opaque objects.','lunar and solar eclipse','images of object in a pinhole camera','diffraction of light','shadows of opque object','','D',1,'',19),(20,'20. The image formed by a convex mirror is always  A. real, erect and diminished      B. real, inverted and diminished      C. virtual, inverted and diminished      D. virtual, erect and diminished','real, erect and diminished','real, inverted and diminished','virtual, inverted and diminished','virtual, erect and diminished','','D',1,'',20);
