INSERT INTO `ss2td3rdtermcat22025quest734` VALUES (1,'?The _________ is the part of a building that transfers the weight of the structure to the ground. a. Floor b. walls c. foundation d. reinforcement','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',1),(2,'When a building is cut or sliced off from the top roof down to the foundation to show clearly the inside portion so as to give sufficient information to the builders it is called ______ A. Bisection B. Construction C.Sectioning D. Distraction','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',2),(3,'Which of the following is a function of a door? a. Provide structural support b. Allow for privacy c. Control temperature d. All of the above','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',3),(4,'A suitable foundation for water-logged soil is the a. Wide strip. b. Pile. c. Pad. d. Deep strip','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',4),(5,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1279310423.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 370px; height: 307px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The figure below shows part of a section through a roof and a wall. The part labelled S is called A. reinforced concrete B. purlin C. wall plate D. lintel&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',5),(6,'Which of the following describes headroom in a stair construction? \nA. Clearance above the stairs to allow easy passage B. Opening into which the stairs is located C. First room at the top of the stairs for access  D. Clearance below the stairs to allow easy passage','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',6),(8,'?How many flights are in the staircase? A. 2 B. 10 C. 11 D. 6','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',8),(9,'The part of a building immediately above a window frame is ___. A. wall plate B. king post C. lintel D.wall','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',9),(10,'Which of the following is not a type of door? A. Raft B. braced C. battened D. ledged','A','B','C','D','','A',0.25,'',10),(11,'?In the double casement window shown below, the stile is labelled as _____.','A','B','C','D','','B',0.25,'',11),(12,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/613646789.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 361px; height: 189px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;?The part of the structural diagram marked A represents A. Coping B. Rafter C. Roofing sheet D. Ridge cap&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',12),(13,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1476785796.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 400px; height: 490px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The part of the structural diagram labeled B is known as a. Block b. Coping c. Threshold d. Cup&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',13),(14,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/1350813591.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 400px; height: 490px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The parts of solid floor include the following except a. hard core b. floor footing c. floor screeds d. concrete over site&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','B',0.25,'',14),(15,'The following are types of foundation except a. Pad b. Raft c. Pile d.  Rad','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',15),(16,'Soffit is a _____member. A. foundation B. floor C. roof D. window ','A','B','C','D','','C',0.25,'',16),(17,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/265501056.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 375px; height: 157px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The symbol above represents a/an a. Arch b. Beam c. Door d. Window&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','D',0.25,'',17),(18,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/801255592.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 375px; height: 122px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The plan of a staircase represented in the diagram above is of what type? a. Straight flight b. dog legged c.Half turn d. Spiral flight&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',18),(19,'&lt;p&gt;&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/231356041.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 384px; height: 268px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;The diagram below shows the front elevation of a building. What type of roof is shown on the building? A.hipped B. lean to C. double lean to D. gable&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','A',0.25,'',19),(20,'?Jambs are member of which of the following building parts? a. Floor b. Door c Wall d. Roof','A','B','C','D','','D',0.25,'',20),(22,'&lt;p style=&quot;margin-left:0pt; margin-right:0pt; text-align:justify&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:10.5pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:Calibri&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:16.0000pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&#039;Times New Roman&#039;&quot;&gt;The part labelled P is the____. A. going B. Tread C. landing D. flight&lt;input alt=&quot;&quot; src=&quot;../../questUploadImages/questionImages/2143279967.png&quot; style=&quot;width: 391px; height: 309px;&quot; type=&quot;image&quot; /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;A&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;B&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;C&lt;/p&gt;\n','&lt;p&gt;D&lt;/p&gt;\n','','C',0.25,'',0);
